...\", \"...\", \"...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Elaborate\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        { \"type\": \"Evaluate\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n**OFFICIAL REB LISTS:**\nUse these exact terms for the \"competences\" field:\n- **Cross-Cutting Issues:** Gender Education, Environmental and sustainability, Peace and Values Education, Inclusive Education, Financial Education, ICT and Digital Literacy.\n- **Generic Competences:** Communication and Collaboration, Critical Thinking and Problem Solving, Creativity and Innovation, Self-Management and Personal Development, Life-long learning.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **FULL CONTENT ONLY:** You MUST populate every single array and field. Never return an empty array.\n2. **EXACT TIMINGS:** Sum of timings (e.g., 10, 24, 6) MUST match exactly 40 min. No ranges.\n3. **REAL HEADER DATA:** The JSON \"header_details\" MUST strictly use the REAL values provided in the INPUT DATA below. Do not invent a different lesson title or duration.\n4. **DEPTH:** Provide dozens of points for the 5Es to ensure a 6-10 page length. Use real subject exercises.\n5. **COMPETENCES FORMAT:** Every item in \"competences\" MUST follow \"Name: Short explanation\". (e.g., \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners solve quadratic equations by...\").\n6. **MAPPING:** Every teacher activity has a direct learner response recorded.\n\n**INPUT DATA:**\n- School: GS KAYONZA\n- Teacher: Demo Teacher\n- Subject: Mathematics\n- Class: \n- Unit: 1 - Introduction To Quadratic Equation\n- Lesson Title: Introduction to linear equations\n- Lesson No: 3\n- Duration: 40 minutes\n- Date: Thu Jan 29 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (Central Africa Time)\n- Term: Term 2\n- Class Size: 40\n- Special Needs: None\n\nGenerate the JSON now:', '[1]', 'groq', 6.436, NULL, '2026-01-28 16:28:16'),
(35, 35, 'You are an expert Rwandan educator. Generate a COMPREHENSIVE lesson plan for the REB curriculum.\n\n**MANDATORY OUTPUT FORMAT:**\nYou must return only a valid JSON object. No other text.\n\n**JSON SCHEMA:**\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"Detailed provision for the specific special needs\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Real title of the unit\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"Real competence from REB syllabus\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Real lesson title\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different communication tools perfectly.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"Location details\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Specific tools\",\n    \"references\": \"Textbooks and pages\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"3-4 sentence overview of lesson\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"A professional reflection statement\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher presents a real-world scenario where...\", \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of...\"],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by...\", \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as...\"],\n          \"competences\": [\"Communication & Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs...\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        { \"type\": \"Explore\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about...\", \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners investigate the puzzle to find...\", \"Learners observe the experiment results and record...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Explain\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher formalizes the concept of X as...\", \"Teacher provides the formula: x² + y² = z² and explains...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners take notes on the definition of X...\", \"Learners apply the formula to solve Example 1...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Elaborate\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher assigns a project where learners must...\", \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners work in groups to design a...\", \"Learners present their arguments for...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        { \n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\", \n          \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is...? Q2: How does...?\", \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve problems 1-5 on page 42.\"], \n          \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A, Q2: Expected Answer: B\", \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask...\"], \n          \"competences\": [\"...\"] \n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n**OFFICIAL REB LISTS:**\nUse these exact terms for the \"competences\" field:\n- **Cross-Cutting Issues:** Gender Education, Environmental and sustainability, Peace and Values Education, Inclusive Education, Financial Education, ICT and Digital Literacy.\n- **Generic Competences:** Communication and Collaboration, Critical Thinking and Problem Solving, Creativity and Innovation, Self-Management and Personal Development, Life-long learning.\n\n**STRICT GENERATION RULES:**\n1. **ABCCD OBJECTIVES:** Every \"instructional_objective\" MUST follow the ABCCD model (Audience, Behavior, Condition, Criteria, Degree) but write it as a natural sentence. DO NOT include parenthetical labels like \"(Audience)\" or \"(Materials)\" in the objective text.\n2. **5Es PEDAGOGICAL RIGOR:**\n   - **Engage:** Use actual hook content (scripts for scenarios, specific brainstorm questions). NO EXPLANATIONS.\n   - **Explore:** Provide specific guided practice text or experiment steps.\n   - **Explain:** Detailed scripted teacher talk with actual content.\n   - **Elaborate:** Real-world complex problems or project briefs.\n   - **Evaluate:** Full Quizzes and Homework with solutions.\n3. **NO PLACEHOLDERS (ACTUAL SCRIPTS MANDATORY):** NEVER describe an activity; you MUST PROVIDE the activity content itself. \n   - **WRONG:** \"Teacher presents a scenario about database inconsistency.\"\n   - **RIGHT:** \"Teacher presents this scenario: \'At a local clinic, a patient\'s medicine was recorded twice with different dosages... Teacher asks: What could happen to the patient?\'\".\n   - This applies to all Scenarios, Examples, Experiments, and Homework.\n4. **DEPTH & VOLUME (CRITICAL):** \n   - You MUST generate at least **10-15 detailed points** for both teacher and learner columns within EVERY sub-phase (Engage, Explore, Explain, Elaborate, Evaluate).\n   - This is necessary to fill 6-10 pages. Do not be brief; be extremely descriptive.\n5. **NESTED FORMATTING:** Use numbering (1., 2., 3.) or sub-bullets (-) inside a single activity point if that point contains a list (like a quiz or multi-step instruction).\n6. **MAPPING:** Every single teacher activity MUST have a direct, detailed response in the learner column.\n7. **COMPETENCES & ISSUES VOLUME:** \n   - For EVERY phase, you MUST identify and explain at least **5-8 distinct Generic Competences and Cross-Cutting Issues** (combine 3-5 from each category).\n   - You must select a variety from both lists. \n   - Each must follow the strict format: \"Name: Detailed explanation of how it is addressed in this specific phase\".\n8. **SUBJECT NOTATION:** Use proper symbols (e.g., x², √x, ≠, π).\n9. **FINAL VALIDATION:** Before returning JSON, double-check: \n   - Does every phase have at least 10 activity points? \n   - Does every phase have 5-8 competences/issues?\n   - Are all scenarios and questions fully written out? \n   - Are objectives ABCCD?\n   - If any check fails, you MUST expand the content before outputting.\n\n**INPUT DATA:**\n- School: GS BUSANZA\n- Teacher: Demo Teacher\n- Subject: Computer Science\n- Class: \n- Unit: 5 - Database Design\n- Lesson Title: Database Optimization Through Normalization\n- Lesson No: 6\n- Duration: 40 minutes\n- Date: Wed Jan 28 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (Central Africa Time)\n- Term: Term 2\n- Class Size: 34\n- Special Needs: 2 with Physical\n\nGenerate the JSON now:', '[]', 'groq', 11.505, NULL, '2026-01-28 17:22:58'),
