ion name provided in input (inside, outside, laboratory, or smartclass) with NO additional text.\n3. **SPECIAL NEEDS PROVISION:** The \"special_needs_provision\" field MUST start by identifying the students (e.g., \"1 student with hearing impairment, 4 slow learners\") and then follow with this exact pedagogic script: \"These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\"\n4. **5Es PEDAGOGICAL RIGOR:**\n   - **Engage:** Use actual hook content (scripts for scenarios, specific brainstorm questions). NO EXPLANATIONS.\n   - **Explore:** Provide specific guided practice text or experiment steps.\n   - **Explain:** Detailed scripted teacher talk with actual content.\n   - **Elaborate:** Real-world complex problems or project briefs.\n   - **Evaluate:** Full Quizzes and Homework. IF YOU PROVIDE MCQs, they must be REAL multiple choice questions with options A, B, C, and D. Never provide an open question if you call it an MCQ.\n5. **NO PLACEHOLDERS (ACTUAL SCRIPTS MANDATORY):** NEVER describe an activity; you MUST PROVIDE the activity content itself (full scenario text, every quiz question, every solution).\n6. **DEPTH & VOLUME (CRITICAL):** You MUST generate at least **10-15 detailed points** for both teacher and learner columns within EVERY sub-phase. Do not be brief.\n7. **COMPETENCES & ISSUES VOLUME:** For EVERY phase, identify and explain at least **5-8 distinct Generic Competences and Cross-Cutting Issues**.\n8. **SUBJECT NOTATION:** Use proper symbols (e.g., x², √x, ≠, π).\n9. **FINAL VALIDATION:** Before returning JSON, double-check: \n   - Does \"plan_for_class\" have extra text? (If yes, remove it).\n   - Are special needs identified and the specific provision script included?\n   - Are MCQs real with A/B/C/D options?\n   - Does every phase have at least 10 activity points and 5-8 competences?\n   - Are objectives ABCCD?\n\n**INPUT DATA:**\n- School: GS BUSANZA\n- Teacher: Demo Teacher\n- Subject: Computer Science\n- Class: \n- Unit: 5 - Database Design\n- Lesson Title: Database Optimization Through Normalization\n- Lesson No: 6\n- Duration: 40 minutes\n- Date: Wed Jan 28 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (Central Africa Time)\n- Term: Term 2\n- Class Size: 34\n- Special Needs: 2 with Physical\n\nGenerate the JSON now:', '[]', 'groq', 8.761, NULL, '2026-01-28 17:31:11');
