eacher_activities\": [\"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about...\", \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners investigate the puzzle to find...\", \"Learners observe the experiment results and record...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Explain\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher formalizes the concept of X as...\", \"Teacher provides the formula: x² + y² = z² and explains...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners take notes on the definition of X...\", \"Learners apply the formula to solve Example 1...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Elaborate\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher assigns a project where learners must...\", \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners work in groups to design a...\", \"Learners present their arguments for...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        { \n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\", \n          \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is...? Q2: How does...?\", \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve problems 1-5 on page 42.\"], \n          \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A, Q2: Expected Answer: B\", \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask...\"], \n          \"competences\": [\"...\"] \n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n**OFFICIAL REB LISTS:**\nUse these exact terms for the \"competences\" field:\n- **Cross-Cutting Issues:** Gender Education, Environmental and sustainability, Peace and Values Education, Inclusive Education, Financial Education, ICT and Digital Literacy.\n- **Generic Competences:** Communication and Collaboration, Critical Thinking and Problem Solving, Creativity and Innovation, Self-Management and Personal Development, Life-long learning.\n\n**STRICT GENERATION RULES:**\n1. **ABCCD OBJECTIVES:** Every \"instructional_objective\" MUST follow the ABCCD model (Audience, Behavior, Condition, Criteria, Degree) as a natural sentence without labels.\n2. **KEY UNIT COMPETENCE FORMAT:** The \"key_unit_competence\" field MUST follow this exact structure with escaped newlines:\n   \"To be able to:\\n. [Action 1]\\n. [Action 2]\"\n   Use a period/dot (.) as the bullet point and \\n for line breaks in the JSON string.\n3. **PLANNED LOCATION:** The \"plan_for_class\" field MUST strictly contain only the location name provided in input (inside, outside, laboratory, or smartclass) with NO additional text.\n4. **TEACHER SELF-EVALUATION:** The \"teacher_self_evaluation\" field MUST be a professional reflection statement in the style of these examples:\n   - \"The lesson was organized and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\"\n   - \"Students were engaged and interested in the lesson, which met the objectives. Next time, I will manage time better and provide additional visual aids.\"\n   - \"The lesson was clear and learners collaborated well during group work. Next time, I will give extra practice exercises to reinforce understanding.\"\n   - \"Learners were motivated and ICT tools helped explain the topic. Next time, I will adjust the pace and add more teaching resources.\"\n   - \"The lesson achieved its goals, and students asked questions and participated actively. Next time, I will focus on including more hands-on activities.\" \n5. **SPECIAL NEEDS PROVISION:** The \"special_needs_provision\" field MUST start by identifying the students (e.g., \"1 student with hearing impairment, 4 slow learners\") and then follow with this exact pedagogic script: \"These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\"\n6. **5Es PEDAGOGICAL RIGOR:**\n    - **Engage:** MANDATORY actual hook content. You MUST write the FULL TEXT of the scenario, the video description, or the specific brainstorm questions. NEVER say \"Teacher presents a scenario about...\". You MUST say \"Teacher presents this scenario: [Full Scenario Text]\".\n   - **Explore:** Provide specific guided practice text or experiment steps.\n   - **Explain:** Detailed scripted teacher talk with actual content.\n   - **Elaborate:** Real-world complex problems or project briefs.\n   - **Evaluate:** Full Quizzes and Homework. IF YOU PROVIDE MCQs, they must be REAL multiple choice questions with options A, B, C, and D. Never provide an open question if you call it an MCQ.\n6. **NO PLACEHOLDERS (ACTUAL SCRIPTS MANDATORY):** NEVER describe an activity; you MUST PROVIDE the activity content itself (full scenario text, every quiz question, every solution). \n   - **MANDATORY FOR ENGAGE:** If you use a scenario, the full story/scenario text MUST be in the Teacher activities column.\n7. **DEPTH & VOLUME (CRITICAL):** You MUST generate at least **10-15 detailed points** for both teacher and learner columns within EVERY sub-phase. Do not be brief.\n8. **COMPETENCES & ISSUES VOLUME:** For EVERY phase, identify and explain at least **5-8 distinct Generic Competences and Cross-Cutting Issues**.\n9. **SUBJECT NOTATION:** Use proper symbols (e.g., x², √x, ≠, π).\n10. **FINAL VALIDATION:** Before returning JSON, double-check: \n    - **ENGAGE CHECK:** Is there a full scenario/hook text? (If it just says \"Teacher presents a scenario\", REGENERATE it with the full text).\n    - Does \"plan_for_class\" have extra text? (If yes, remove it).\n    - Are special needs identified and the specific provision script included?\n    - Are MCQs real with A/B/C/D options?\n    - Does every phase have at least 10 activity points and 5-8 competences?\n    - Are objectives ABCCD?\n    - Is the self-evaluation professional, reflective, and following the provided style?\n\n**INPUT DATA:**\n- School: G.S BUSANZA\n- Teacher: Demo Teacher\n- Subject: Computer Science\n- Class: \n- Unit: 6 - Pointer and structure\n- Lesson Title: introduction to pointer\n- Lesson No: 1\n- Duration: 80 minutes\n- Date: Fri Jan 30 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (Central Africa Time)\n- Term: Term 2\n- Class Size: 34\n- Special Needs: 2 with Visual\n\n\n**PRIMARY REFERENCE MATERIALS (BOOKS/DOCUMENTS):**\nThe following content is extracted from official books or documents uploaded by the teacher. You MUST use this as your PRIMARY source for the lesson content, examples, and activities.\n\n--- MATERIAL 1: Computer ---\n\n\nCOMPUTER SCIENCE S5\nSTUDENT\'S BOOK\n\nCopyright \n© 2022 Rwanda Basic Education Board\nAll rights reserved.\nThis book is the property of the Government of Rwanda. \nCredit should be given to REB when the source of this book is quoted\n\nii\nComputer Science Senior 5 StudentBook\nCopyright \n© 2019 Rwanda Basic Education Board\nAll rights reserved.\nThis document is the property of Rwanda Basic Education \nBoard. \nComputer Science Senior 5   Student’s Book\nii\niii\nComputer Science Senior 5 Student Book\nFOREWORD\nDear Student,\nRwanda Basic Education Board is honoured to present to you this Computer Science\nbook for  Senior  ve  which  serves  as  a  guide  to  competence-based  teaching  and  \nlearning to ensure consistency and coherence in the learning of Computer Science \nsubject.  The  Rwandan  educational  philosophy  is  to  ensure  that  you  achieve  full \npotential at every level of education which will prepare you to be well integrated in \nsociety and exploit employment opportunities.  \nThe  government  of  Rwanda  emphasizes  the  importance  of  aligning  teaching  and \nlearning materials with the syllabus to facilitate your learning process. Many factors \nThose  factors  include  the  instructional  materials  available  among  others.  Special \nattention  to  the  activities  that  facilitate  the  learning  process  in  which  you  can \ndevelop your ideas and make new discoveries during concrete activities carried out \nindividually or with peers. \nIn  competence-based  curriculum,  learning  is  considered  as  a  process\n  of  active \nbuilding and developing knowledge and meanings by the learner where concepts \nare mainly introduced by an activity, a situation or a scenario that helps the learner \nto  construct  knowledge,  develop  skills  and  acquire  positive  attitudes  and  values. \nFor eective use of this textbook, your role is to:\n•Work on given activities which lead to the development of skills\n•Share relevant information with other learners through presentations,\ndiscussions, group work and other active learning techniques such as\nrole play, case studies, investigation and research in the library, from the\ninternet or from your community;\n•Participate and take responsibility for your own learning;\nI wish to sincerely extend my appreciation to the people who contributed towards \nprocess  from  its  inception.  Special gratitude  goes  to  the  University  of  Rwanda \nwhich provided experts in design and layout services, illustrations and image anti-\nplagiarism, lecturers and teachers who diligently worked to successful completion \nof this book. Any comment or contribution would be welcome for the improvement \nof this textbook for the next edition.  \nDr. MBARUSHIMANA Nelson \nDirector General, REB\niii\nComputer Science  Senior 5  Student’s Book\n\niv\nComputer Science Senior 5 Student Book\n ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\nI  wish  to  express  my  appreciation  to  all  the  people  who  played  a  major  role  in  \ndevelopment  of  this  textbook.  It  wou\n\n\nCRITICAL: While you prioritize the above materials, you are encouraged to use your general expert knowledge to enhance the introduction, development, and conclusion, provided it does NOT contradict the provided materials.\n\nGenerate the JSON now:', '[]', 'groq', 7.799, NULL, '2026-01-29 15:53:29'),
(52, 16, 'You are an expert Rwandan educator. Generate a COMPREHENSIVE lesson plan for the REB curriculum.\n\n**MANDATORY OUTPUT FORMAT:**\nYou must return only a valid JSON object. No other text.\nCRITICAL: All string values in JSON MUST use escaped characters (\\n for newlines, \\t for tabs). Never use literal newlines inside JSON string values.\n\n**JSON SCHEMA:**\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"Detailed provision for the specific special needs\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Real title of the unit\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Real lesson title\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different communication tools perfectly.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"Location details\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Specific tools\",\n    \"references\": \"Textbooks and pages\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"3-4 sentence overview of lesson\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"A professional reflection statement\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher presents a real-world scenario where...\", \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of...\"],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by...\", \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as...\"],\n          \"competences\": [\"Communication & Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs...\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        { \"type\": \"Explore\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about...\", \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners investigate the puzzle to find...\", \"Learners observe the experiment results and record...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Explain\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher formalizes the concept of X as...\", \"Teacher provides the formula: x² + y² = z² and explains...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners take notes on the definition of X...\", \"Learners apply the formula to solve Example 1...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] },\n        { \"type\": \"Elaborate\", \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher assigns a project where learners must...\", \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of...\"], \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners work in groups to design a...\", \"Learners present their arguments for...\"], \"competences\": [\"...\"] }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        { \n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\", \n          \"teacher_activities\": [\"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is...? Q2: How does...?\", \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve problems 1-5 on page 42.\"], \n          \"learner_activities\": [\"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A, Q2: Expected Answer: B\", \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask...\"], \n          \"competences\": [\"...\"] \n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n**OFFICIAL REB LISTS:**\nUse these exact terms for the \"competences\" field:\n- **Cross-Cutting Issues:** Gender Education, Environmental and sustainability, Peace and Values Education, Inclusive Education, Financial Education, ICT and Digital Literacy.\n- **Generic Competences:** Communication and Collaboration, Critical Thinking and Problem Solving, Creativity and Innovation, Self-Management and Personal Development, Life-long learning.\n\n**STRICT GENERATION RULES:**\n1. **ABCCD OBJECTIVES:** Every \"instructional_objective\" MUST follow the ABCCD model (Audience, Behavior, Condition, Criteria, Degree) as a natural sentence without labels.\n2. **KEY UNIT COMPETENCE FORMAT:** The \"key_unit_competence\" field MUST follow this exact structure with escaped newlines:\n   \"To be able to:\\n. [Action 1]\\n. [Action 2]\"\n   Use a period/dot (.) as the bullet point and \\n for line breaks in the JSON string.\n3. **PLANNED LOCATION:** The \"plan_for_class\" field MUST strictly contain only the location name provided in input (inside, outside, laboratory, or smartclass) with NO additional text.\n4. **TEACHER SELF-EVALUATION:** The \"teacher_self_evaluation\" field MUST be a professional reflection statement in the style of these examples:\n   - \"The lesson was organized and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\"\n   - \"Students were engaged and interested in the lesson, which met the objectives. Next time, I will manage time better and provide additional visual aids.\"\n   - \"The lesson was clear and learners collaborated well during group work. Next time, I will give extra practice exercises to reinforce understanding.\"\n   - \"Learners were motivated and ICT tools helped explain the topic. Next time, I will adjust the pace and add more teaching resources.\"\n   - \"The lesson achieved its goals, and students asked questions and participated actively. Next time, I will focus on including more hands-on activities.\" \n5. **SPECIAL NEEDS PROVISION:** The \"special_needs_provision\" field MUST start by identifying the students (e.g., \"1 student with hearing impairment, 4 slow learners\") and then follow with this exact pedagogic script: \"These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\"\n6. **5Es PEDAGOGICAL RIGOR:**\n    - **Engage:** MANDATORY actual hook content. You MUST write the FULL TEXT of the scenario, the video description, or the specific brainstorm questions. NEVER say \"Teacher presents a scenario about...\". You MUST say \"Teacher presents this scenario: [Full Scenario Text]\".\n   - **Explore:** Provide specific guided practice text or experiment steps.\n   - **Explain:** Detailed scripted teacher talk with actual content.\n   - **Elaborate:** Real-world complex problems or project briefs.\n   - **Evaluate:** Full Quizzes and Homework. IF YOU PROVIDE MCQs, they must be REAL multiple choice questions with options A, B, C, and D. Never provide an open question if you call it an MCQ.\n6. **NO PLACEHOLDERS (ACTUAL SCRIPTS MANDATORY):** NEVER describe an activity; you MUST PROVIDE the activity content itself (full scenario text, every quiz question, every solution). \n   - **MANDATORY FOR ENGAGE:** If you use a scenario, the full story/scenario text MUST be in the Teacher activities column.\n7. **DEPTH & VOLUME (CRITICAL):** You MUST generate at least **10-15 detailed points** for both teacher and learner columns within EVERY sub-phase. Do not be brief.\n8. **COMPETENCES & ISSUES VOLUME:** For EVERY phase, identify and explain at least **5-8 distinct Generic Competences and Cross-Cutting Issues**.\n9. **SUBJECT NOTATION:** Use proper symbols (e.g., x², √x, ≠, π).\n10. **FINAL VALIDATION:** Before returning JSON, double-check: \n    - **ENGAGE CHECK:** Is there a full scenario/hook text? (If it just says \"Teacher presents a scenario\", REGENERATE it with the full text).\n    - Does \"plan_for_class\" have extra text? (If yes, remove it).\n    - Are special needs identified and the specific provision script included?\n    - Are MCQs real with A/B/C/D options?\n    - Does every phase have at least 10 activity points and 5-8 competences?\n    - Are objectives ABCCD?\n    - Is the self-evaluation professional, reflective, and following the provided style?\n\n**INPUT DATA:**\n- School: G.S BUSANZA\n- Teacher: Demo Teacher\n- Subject: Computer Science\n- Class: \n- Unit: 6 - Pointer and structure\n- Lesson Title: introduction to pointer\n- Lesson No: 1\n- Duration: 80 minutes\n- Date: Fri Jan 30 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (Central Africa Time)\n- Term: Term 2\n- Class Size: 34\n- Special Needs: 2 with Visual\n\n\n**PRIMARY REFERENCE MATERIALS (BOOKS/DOCUMENTS):**\nThe following content is extracted from official books or documents uploaded by the teacher. You MUST use this as your PRIMARY source for the lesson content, examples, and activities.\n\n--- MATERIAL 1: Computer ---\n\n\nCOMPUTER SCIENCE S5\nSTUDENT\'S BOOK\n\nCopyright \n© 2022 Rwanda Basic Education Board\nAll rights reserved.\nThis book is the property of the Government of Rwanda. \nCredit should be given to REB when the source of this book is quoted\n\nii\nComputer Science Senior 5 StudentBook\nCopyright \n© 2019 Rwanda Basic Education Board\nAll rights reserved.\nThis document is the property of Rwanda Basic Education \nBoard. \nComputer Science Senior 5   Student’s Book\nii\niii\nComputer Science Senior 5 Student Book\nFOREWORD\nDear Student,\nRwanda Basic Education Board is honoured to present to you this Computer Science\nbook for  Senior  ve  which  serves  as  a  guide  to  competence-based  teaching  and  \nlearning to ensure consistency and coherence in the learning of Computer Science \nsubject.  The  Rwandan  educational  philosophy  is  to  ensure  that  you  achieve  full \npotential at every level of education which will prepare you to be well integrated in \nsociety and exploit employment opportunities.  \nThe  government  of  Rwanda  emphasizes  the  importance  of  aligning  teaching  and \nlearning materials with the syllabus to facilitate your learning process. Many factors \nThose  factors  include  the  instructional  materials  available  among  others.  Special \nattention  to  the  activities  that  facilitate  the  learning  process  in  which  you  can \ndevelop your ideas and make new discoveries during concrete activities carried out \nindividually or with peers. \nIn  competence-based  curriculum,  learning  is  considered  as  a  process\n  of  active \nbuilding and developing knowledge and meanings by the learner where concepts \nare mainly introduced by an activity, a situation or a scenario that helps the learner \nto  construct  knowledge,  develop  skills  and  acquire  positive  attitudes  and  values. \nFor eective use of this textbook, your role is to:\n•Work on given activities which lead to the development of skills\n•Share relevant information with other learners through presentations,\ndiscussions, group work and other active learning techniques such as\nrole play, case studies, investigation and research in the library, from the\ninternet or from your community;\n•Participate and take responsibility for your own learning;\nI wish to sincerely extend my appreciation to the people who contributed towards \nprocess  from  its  inception.  Special gratitude  goes  to  the  University  of  Rwanda \nwhich provided experts in design and layout services, illustrations and image anti-\nplagiarism, lecturers and teachers who diligently worked to successful completion \nof this book. Any comment or contribution would be welcome for the improvement \nof this textbook for the next edition.  \nDr. MBARUSHIMANA Nelson \nDirector General, REB\niii\nComputer Science  Senior 5  Student’s Book\n\niv\nComputer Science Senior 5 Student Book\n ACKNOWLEDGEMENT\nI  wish  to  express  my  appreciation  to  all  the  people  who  played  a  major  role  in  \ndevelopment  of  this  textbook.  It  wou\n\n\nCRITICAL: While you prioritize the above materials, you are encouraged to use your general expert knowledge to enhance the introduction, development, and conclusion, provided it does NOT contradict the provided materials.\n\nGenerate the JSON now:', '[]', 'groq', 9.035, NULL, '2026-01-29 16:03:40');
