e, Explore, Explain, Elaborate, Evaluate). There is a hard FLOOR of at least **5 points** per column per sub-phase. Do not be brief.\n8. **COMPETENCES & ISSUES ACCURACY (NO DUPLICATION):** \n    - **CLEAN LABELING:** Use ONLY the official name from the REB lists (e.g., \"Gender Education\", \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving\") followed by a colon and the description. \n    - **PROHIBITED:** Do NOT include the category headers \"Cross-Cutting Issues:\" or \"Generic Competences:\" inside the strings themselves. \n    - **NO DUPLICATION:** Every competence or issue in a phase must be unique. Do not repeat the same one.\n    - **REB LISTS:** Match the spelling of the official lists exactly.\n9. **SUBJECT NOTATION:** Use proper symbols (e.g., x², √x, ≠, π).\n10. **FINAL VALIDATION:** Before returning JSON, double-check: \n    - **ENGAGE CHECK:** Is there a full scenario/hook text?\n    - **ASSESSMENT CHECK:** Are questions set using Bloom\'s Taxonomy? Are all exercises, quizzes, and homework questions written out in full? (If it says \"Teacher gives a quiz on...\" or \"Complete page X...\", REGENERATE it to include the actual questions word-for-word).\n    - **VOLUME CHECK:** Does every column in every sub-phase have at least 5-10 detailed activity points? (If less, add more).\n    - **COMPETENCE CHECK:** Are Generic Competences and Cross-Cutting Issues correctly labeled and NOT duplicated?\n    - Does \"plan_for_class\" have extra text?\n    - Are special needs identified and the specific provision script included?\n    - Are MCQs real with A/B/C/D options?\n    - Are objectives ABCCD?\n    - Is the self-evaluation professional, reflective, and following the provided style?\n\n**INPUT DATA:**\n- School: RUKARA MODEL SCHOOL\n- Teacher: Eline MUKANDAYISENGA\n- Subject: English\n- Class: \n- Unit: 6 - HEALTH LIVING\n- Lesson Title: LANGUAGES STRACTURE \n- Lesson No: 3\n- Duration: 80 minutes\n- Date: Fri Jan 30 2026 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (Central Africa Time)\n- Term: Te