(12, 4, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with physical disabilities will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold these students through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Database Design\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different database terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply database concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Database Optimization Through Normalization\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and database software, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different database normalization techniques perfectly, given the database schema and data, with at least 90% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, database software, and internet connection\",\n    \"references\": \"Database Systems textbook, pages 120-130\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to database normalization techniques to optimize database design. Students will learn about the different normalization rules and how to apply them to a given database schema. The lesson will include hands-on activities and quizzes to assess student understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured, and students participated actively in the hands-on activities. Most students understood the concepts of database normalization. Next time, I will include more examples and provide additional support to slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A company has a database with customer information, orders, and products. However, the database is not normalized, and data redundancy is causing errors. The company wants to optimize the database design to improve data integrity and reduce errors.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a database schema and explains the concept of data redundancy and normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm the problems that can occur in a database with redundant data.\",\n            \"Teacher writes the brainstormed ideas on the chalkboard and discusses them with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher introduces the concept of database normalization and its importance in database design.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the different normalization rules, including 1NF, 2NF, and 3NF.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of each normalization rule and asks students to identify which rule is being applied.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the benefits of database normalization, including improved data integrity and reduced errors.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a sample database schema and asks students to identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe the animation video and take notes on the concept of data redundancy and normalization.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the brainstorming activity and share their ideas with the class.\",\n            \"Learners listen to the teacher\'s explanation of database normalization and take notes.\",\n            \"Learners identify the normalization rules being applied in the examples provided by the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied to the sample database schema.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their findings with the class and explain their reasoning.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher for feedback on their understanding of the concepts.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and make sure they understand the key concepts.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their ideas with the class.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the sample database schema and identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can improve their understanding.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - The teacher ensures that all students, regardless of gender, have an equal opportunity to participate in the brainstorming activity.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - The teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it can be achieved through normalization, which can help reduce errors and improve data integrity.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - The teacher promotes a culture of respect and inclusivity in the classroom, encouraging all students to participate and share their ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - The teacher provides accommodations for students with physical disabilities, such as using radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about database normalization and asks students to solve it.\",\n            \"Teacher guides students through an experiment where they have to normalize a given database schema.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of functional dependencies and how they are used in normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of functional dependencies and asks students to identify them.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the importance of normalization in reducing data redundancy and improving data integrity.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a sample database schema and asks students to identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the benefits of database normalization, including improved data integrity and reduced errors.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a case study of a company that implemented database normalization and asks students to analyze the benefits.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners solve the puzzle and submit their answers to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the experiment and normalize the given database schema.\",\n            \"Learners identify the functional dependencies in the examples provided by the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied to the sample database schema.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their findings with the class and explain their reasoning.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher for feedback on their understanding of the concepts.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and make sure they understand the key concepts.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and discuss the benefits of database normalization.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the sample database schema and identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can improve their understanding.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - The teacher ensures that all students, regardless of gender, have an equal opportunity to participate in the experiment.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - The teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it can be achieved through normalization, which can help reduce errors and improve data integrity.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - The teacher promotes a culture of respect and inclusivity in the classroom, encouraging all students to participate and share their ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - The teacher provides accommodations for students with physical disabilities, such as using radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of database normalization and explains the different normalization rules.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of each normalization rule and asks students to identify which rule is being applied.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of functional dependencies and how they are used in normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of functional dependencies and asks students to identify them.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the importance of normalization in reducing data redundancy and improving data integrity.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a sample database schema and asks students to identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the benefits of database normalization, including improved data integrity and reduced errors.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a case study of a company that implemented database normalization and asks students to analyze the benefits.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of database normalization and the different normalization rules.\",\n            \"Learners identify the normalization rules being applied in the examples provided by the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied to the sample database schema.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their findings with the class and explain their reasoning.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher for feedback on their understanding of the concepts.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and make sure they understand the key concepts.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and discuss the benefits of database normalization.\",\n            \"Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the sample database schema and identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can improve their understanding.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - The teacher ensures that all students, regardless of gender, have an equal opportunity to participate in the discussion.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - The teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it can be achieved through normalization, which can help reduce errors and improve data integrity.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - The teacher promotes a culture of respect and inclusivity in the classroom, encouraging all students to participate and share their ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - The teacher provides accommodations for students with physical disabilities, such as using radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design a database for a given scenario.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidelines and requirements for the project.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the expectations and the criteria for evaluation.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of database designs and asks students to identify the normalization rules that are being applied.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data redundancy and how it can be reduced through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a case study of a company that implemented database normalization and asks students to analyze the benefits.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the benefits of database normalization, including improved data integrity and reduced errors.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to students as they work on the project.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners design a database for the given scenario and submit it to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied to their database design.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their findings with the class and explain their reasoning.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher for feedback on their understanding of the concepts.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and make sure they understand the key concepts.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and discuss the benefits of database normalization.\",\n            \"Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners work on the project and submit it to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners receive feedback and guidance from the teacher and revise their project accordingly.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the sample database schema and identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can improve their understanding.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - The teacher ensures that all students, regardless of gender, have an equal opportunity to participate in the project.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - The teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it can be achieved through normalization, which can help reduce errors and improve data integrity.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - The teacher promotes a culture of respect and inclusivity in the classroom, encouraging all students to participate and share their ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - The teacher provides accommodations for students with physical disabilities, such as using radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz: Q1: What is the purpose of database normalization? A) To reduce data redundancy, B) To improve data integrity, C) To increase data storage, D) To decrease data retrieval time.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the answers to the quiz and discusses the correct answers.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Design a database for a given scenario and apply the normalization rules learned in class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to students as they work on the homework.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the benefits of database normalization and how it can be applied to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data consistency and how it is achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a case study of a company that implemented database normalization and asks students to analyze the benefits.\",\n            \"Teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it can be achieved through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a summary of the key concepts learned in class.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions and submit their answers to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners discuss the correct answers with the class and explain their reasoning.\",\n            \"Learners work on the homework and submit it to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners receive feedback and guidance from the teacher and revise their homework accordingly.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and discuss the benefits of database normalization.\",\n            \"Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can improve their understanding.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher for feedback on their understanding of the concepts.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and make sure they understand the key concepts.\",\n            \"Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss the correct answers with the class and explain their reasoning.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the sample database schema and identify the normalization rules that can be applied.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how they can apply database normalization to real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and think about how they can improve their understanding.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - The teacher ensures that all students, regardless of gender, have an equal opportunity to participate in the quiz.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - The teacher discusses the importance of data consistency and how it can be achieved through normalization, which can help reduce errors and improve data integrity.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - The teacher promotes a culture of respect and inclusivity in the classroom, encouraging all students to participate and share their ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - The teacher provides accommodations for students with physical disabilities, such as using radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 12, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 14:21:17', '2026-01-29 14:21:17'),
(13, 4, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with physical disabilities will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold these students through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Database Design\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different database terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply database concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Database Optimization Through Normalization\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and database software, at the end of this lesson, every student in the class will be able to identify and state the use of different normalization techniques perfectly, under the condition of having access to the internet and a computer, with a degree of 90% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, database software, internet connection\",\n    \"references\": \"Database Systems textbook, pages 120-130\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"The lesson will start with an introduction to database normalization, followed by an exploration of the different normalization techniques. The teacher will explain the concepts and provide examples, and the learners will work in groups to practice normalizing databases. The lesson will conclude with an evaluation of the learners\' understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and learners participated actively in the group work. Most learners understood the concepts of normalization, but some struggled with applying them. Next time, I will provide more examples and practice exercises to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A company has a database that stores information about its employees, including their names, addresses, and salaries. However, the database is not normalized, and this is causing problems when trying to update the information. For example, if an employee moves to a new address, the address needs to be updated in multiple places, which can lead to inconsistencies.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a database being normalized, with a voiceover explaining the process.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to brainstorm the benefits of normalizing a database, such as reducing data redundancy and improving data integrity.\",\n            \"Teacher writes the brainstormed ideas on the chalkboard and asks learners to discuss them in pairs.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a diagram of a normalized database and asks learners to identify the different tables and their relationships.\",\n            \"Teacher explains that normalization is the process of organizing the data in a database to minimize data redundancy and dependency.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a simple example of a normalized database, such as a customer database with separate tables for customers, orders, and products.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to match the different normalization techniques with their definitions, such as first normal form (1NF), second normal form (2NF), and third normal form (3NF).\",\n            \"Teacher provides a worksheet with a set of questions related to database normalization, such as What is the purpose of normalization? and What are the benefits of normalizing a database?\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to complete the worksheet and then discuss their answers in small groups.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe the animation video and take notes on the process of normalizing a database.\",\n            \"Learners brainstorm the benefits of normalizing a database and write them down on a piece of paper.\",\n            \"Learners discuss the brainstormed ideas in pairs and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different tables and their relationships in the diagram of a normalized database.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the example of a normalized database and provide feedback to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the different normalization techniques with their definitions.\",\n            \"Learners complete the worksheet with questions related to database normalization.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their answers in small groups and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher questions about any concepts they do not understand.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners brainstorm the benefits of normalizing a database and identify the different tables and their relationships.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to normalize a database and provide new ideas.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and brainstorming activities.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners are encouraged to think about the environmental impact of data storage and the importance of efficient data management.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners are encouraged to respect each other\'s opinions and ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - Learners with physical disabilities are provided with accommodations, such as the use of radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about normalizing a database, such as a set of tables with redundant data.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they have to normalize a sample database, using a step-by-step approach.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of data redundancy and how it can be eliminated through normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of examples of normalized databases, such as a customer database with separate tables for customers, orders, and products.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to identify the different normalization techniques used in the examples, such as first normal form (1NF), second normal form (2NF), and third normal form (3NF).\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of questions related to database normalization, such as What is the purpose of normalization? and What are the benefits of normalizing a database?\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to complete the questions and then discuss their answers in small groups.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to learners on their understanding of database normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources, such as a video or a website, for learners to learn more about database normalization.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the puzzle and normalize the database.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the experiment and normalize the sample database.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the concept of data redundancy and how it can be eliminated.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different normalization techniques used in the examples.\",\n            \"Learners complete the questions related to database normalization.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their answers in small groups and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher questions about any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to create a simple normalized database, using a database software.\",\n            \"Learners present their normalized database to the class and provide feedback to each other.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to solve the puzzle and normalize the database.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners participate in the experiment and normalize the sample database.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to normalize a database and provide new ideas.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and brainstorming activities.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners are encouraged to think about the environmental impact of data storage and the importance of efficient data management.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners are encouraged to respect each other\'s opinions and ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - Learners with physical disabilities are provided with accommodations, such as the use of radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of normalization as the process of organizing the data in a database to minimize data redundancy and dependency.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for normalizing a database, such as the use of primary keys and foreign keys.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the different normalization techniques, such as first normal form (1NF), second normal form (2NF), and third normal form (3NF).\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of normalized databases, such as a customer database with separate tables for customers, orders, and products.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to identify the different normalization techniques used in the examples.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of questions related to database normalization, such as What is the purpose of normalization? and What are the benefits of normalizing a database?\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to complete the questions and then discuss their answers in small groups.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to learners on their understanding of database normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources, such as a video or a website, for learners to learn more about database normalization.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of normalization and the formula for normalizing a database.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the different normalization techniques and how they are used.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different normalization techniques used in the examples.\",\n            \"Learners complete the questions related to database normalization.\",\n            \"Learners discuss their answers in small groups and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher questions about any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to create a simple normalized database, using a database software.\",\n            \"Learners present their normalized database to the class and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners evaluate the effectiveness of the normalization techniques used in the examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to identify the different normalization techniques used in the examples.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners participate in the discussion and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to normalize a database and provide new ideas.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and brainstorming activities.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners are encouraged to think about the environmental impact of data storage and the importance of efficient data management.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners are encouraged to respect each other\'s opinions and ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - Learners with physical disabilities are provided with accommodations, such as the use of radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design and implement a normalized database for a real-world scenario, such as a customer database for an e-commerce website.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support to learners as they work on the project.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to think creatively about how to normalize the database and provide new ideas.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to present their project to the class and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources, such as a video or a website, for learners to learn more about database normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to learners on their understanding of database normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Teacher provides opportunities for learners to work in pairs or small groups to complete the project.\",\n            \"Teacher evaluates the effectiveness of the project and provides feedback to learners.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in pairs or small groups to design and implement the normalized database.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Learners present their project to the class and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Learners evaluate the effectiveness of the project and provide feedback to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs or small groups to complete the project and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher questions about any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to the teacher on the effectiveness of the project and the learning experience.\",\n            \"Learners evaluate the project and provide recommendations for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs or small groups to complete the project.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners participate in the project and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to normalize the database and provide new ideas.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and brainstorming activities.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners are encouraged to think about the environmental impact of data storage and the importance of efficient data management.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners are encouraged to respect each other\'s opinions and ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - Learners with physical disabilities are provided with accommodations, such as the use of radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz: Q1: What is the purpose of normalization? A) To reduce data redundancy, B) To increase data dependency, C) To improve data security, D) To reduce data storage.\",\n            \"Q2: What is the benefit of normalizing a database? A) Improved data integrity, B) Reduced data redundancy, C) Improved data security, D) All of the above.\",\n            \"Q3: What is the formula for normalizing a database? A) Primary key + foreign key, B) Primary key - foreign key, C) Primary key x foreign key, D) Primary key / foreign key.\",\n            \"Q4: What is the difference between first normal form (1NF) and second normal form (2NF)? A) 1NF eliminates repeating groups, while 2NF eliminates partial dependencies.\",\n            \"Q5: What is the benefit of using a normalized database? A) Improved data integrity, B) Reduced data redundancy, C) Improved data security, D) All of the above.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Complete the exercises on pages 120-130 of the Database Systems textbook.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to learners on their understanding of database normalization.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Teacher evaluates the effectiveness of the lesson and provides feedback to learners.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the multiple-choice quiz questions and provide feedback to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework exercises and provide feedback to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher questions about any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to the teacher on the effectiveness of the lesson and the learning experience.\",\n            \"Learners evaluate the lesson and provide recommendations for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs or small groups to complete the homework exercises and provide feedback to each other.\",\n            \"Learners ask the teacher questions about any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to the teacher on the effectiveness of the homework exercises and the learning experience.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it to real-world scenarios.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs or small groups to complete the homework exercises.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners participate in the quiz and provide feedback to the teacher.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to normalize a database and provide new ideas.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher and their peers.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and brainstorming activities.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners are encouraged to think about the environmental impact of data storage and the importance of efficient data management.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners are encouraged to respect each other\'s opinions and ideas.\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Inclusive Education - Learners with physical disabilities are provided with accommodations, such as the use of radio connected to the computer for audio and video.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 13, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 15:50:20', '2026-01-29 15:50:20');
INSERT INTO `lesson_plans` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `content`, `version`, `generated_by_ai`, `ai_provider`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(15, 5, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with visual impairment will be helped by using computers connected to a projector for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Unit 6 - Pointer and Structure\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of pointers in programming\\n. Apply pointers to solve problems and develop algorithms\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Introduction to Pointer\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and programming software, every student will be able to define and explain the concept of pointers in programming, apply pointers to solve problems and develop algorithms, under the guidance of the teacher, with at least 80% accuracy, by the end of the lesson.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"smartclass\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, programming software, projectors, and whiteboards\",\n    \"references\": \"Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book, pages 100-120\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces the concept of pointers in programming, explaining their definition, application, and importance in developing algorithms. Students will engage in activities to understand and apply pointers, and the teacher will provide guidance and feedback throughout the lesson. The lesson will cover the basics of pointers, including declaration, initialization, and usage, and will include hands-on practice and group discussions to reinforce understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and students participated actively in the discussions and activities. Most students understood the concept of pointers, but some struggled with applying them to solve problems. Next time, I will include more examples and practice exercises to support slower learners and provide additional feedback to students.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a programmer working on a project that requires you to store and manipulate large amounts of data. You need to use pointers to efficiently manage memory and improve performance.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of how pointers work in programming, explaining the concept of memory addresses and pointer variables.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm and discuss the following questions: What are pointers? Why are they important in programming? How do they work?\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a simple programming example that demonstrates the use of pointers, and asks students to work in pairs to understand and explain the code.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and share their thoughts on the scenario and video, and provides guidance and feedback on their understanding.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario, identifying the key elements and challenges of using pointers in programming.\",\n            \"Learners watch the animation video and take notes on the concept of pointers and memory addresses.\",\n            \"Learners brainstorm and discuss the questions, sharing their thoughts and ideas with the class.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to understand and explain the programming example, using the handout and their own notes.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher, clarifying any doubts or misconceptions.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss and share their thoughts and ideas with the class.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and video, identifying the key elements and challenges of using pointers.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners brainstorm and generate new ideas and solutions to the programming example.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, seeking feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners demonstrate a willingness to learn and understand new concepts, asking questions and seeking clarification.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with exercises on declaring and initializing pointers, and asks students to work in pairs to complete the exercises.\",\n            \"Teacher guides students through an experiment where they use programming software to demonstrate the use of pointers, explaining the concept of pointer arithmetic and memory allocation.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a programming example that demonstrates the use of pointers to solve a real-world problem, and asks students to work in groups to understand and explain the code.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek feedback on their understanding, providing guidance and support as needed.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the whiteboard to illustrate the concept of pointers, explaining the relationship between pointer variables and memory addresses.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete the exercises, using the worksheets and their own notes to understand the concept of declaring and initializing pointers.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the experiment, using the programming software to demonstrate the use of pointers and pointer arithmetic.\",\n            \"Learners work in groups to understand and explain the programming example, using the handout and their own notes.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher, clarifying any doubts or misconceptions.\",\n            \"Learners use the whiteboard to illustrate their understanding of pointers, explaining the relationship between pointer variables and memory addresses.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs and groups to complete exercises and understand programming examples.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve problems using pointers, demonstrating an understanding of pointer arithmetic and memory allocation.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners generate new ideas and solutions to programming problems, using pointers to efficiently manage memory and improve performance.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, seeking feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners demonstrate a willingness to learn and understand new concepts, asking questions and seeking clarification.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of pointers, explaining the definition and syntax of pointer variables.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for pointer arithmetic, explaining how to calculate memory addresses and pointer values.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the whiteboard to illustrate the relationship between pointer variables and memory addresses, explaining the concept of pointer aliasing.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how pointers are used in real-world programming applications, explaining the benefits and challenges of using pointers.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek feedback on their understanding, providing guidance and support as needed.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition and syntax of pointer variables, using the handout and their own notes.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to practice calculating memory addresses and pointer values, using the formula and their own notes.\",\n            \"Learners use the whiteboard to illustrate their understanding of pointer aliasing, explaining the relationship between pointer variables and memory addresses.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher, clarifying any doubts or misconceptions.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of pointers, identifying areas where they need more practice or review.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to practice calculating memory addresses and pointer values.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve problems using pointers, demonstrating an understanding of pointer arithmetic and memory allocation.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners generate new ideas and solutions to programming problems, using pointers to efficiently manage memory and improve performance.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, seeking feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners demonstrate a willingness to learn and understand new concepts, asking questions and seeking clarification.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must develop a programming application that uses pointers to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support as needed, encouraging learners to ask questions and seek feedback.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the whiteboard to illustrate the concept of dynamic memory allocation, explaining how pointers are used to manage memory in programming applications.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how pointers are used in different programming languages, explaining the benefits and challenges of using pointers in each language.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to reflect on their understanding of pointers, identifying areas where they need more practice or review.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to develop the programming application, using pointers to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher, clarifying any doubts or misconceptions.\",\n            \"Learners use the whiteboard to illustrate their understanding of dynamic memory allocation, explaining how pointers are used to manage memory in programming applications.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of pointers, identifying areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Learners present their programming application to the class, explaining how they used pointers to solve the real-world problem.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in groups to develop the programming application.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve problems using pointers, demonstrating an understanding of pointer arithmetic and memory allocation.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners generate new ideas and solutions to programming problems, using pointers to efficiently manage memory and improve performance.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, seeking feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners demonstrate a willingness to learn and understand new concepts, asking questions and seeking clarification.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz to assess learners\' understanding of pointers, with questions such as: What is the definition of a pointer? How do you declare and initialize a pointer? What is the purpose of pointer arithmetic?\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Complete exercises on pages 100-120 of the Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book, and develop a short programming application that demonstrates the use of pointers.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to reflect on their understanding of pointers, identifying areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners, addressing any doubts or misconceptions.\",\n            \"Teacher summarizes the key points of the lesson, explaining the importance of pointers in programming and the benefits of using them to efficiently manage memory and improve performance.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners complete the multiple-choice quiz, using their notes and the handout to answer the questions.\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework exercises, using the Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book and their own notes.\",\n            \"Learners develop the short programming application, using pointers to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of pointers, identifying areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher, clarifying any doubts or misconceptions.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to complete the homework exercises.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve problems using pointers, demonstrating an understanding of pointer arithmetic and memory allocation.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners generate new ideas and solutions to programming problems, using pointers to efficiently manage memory and improve performance.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, seeking feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners demonstrate a willingness to learn and understand new concepts, asking questions and seeking clarification.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 2, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 15:53:29', '2026-01-29 15:53:29'),
(16, 5, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with visual impairment, These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Unit 6 - Pointer and Structure\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of pointers in programming\\n. Use pointers to manipulate data in a program\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Introduction to Pointer\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and programming software, students with prior knowledge of basic programming concepts, will be able to define and explain the concept of pointers, and use pointers to manipulate data in a program, with 80% accuracy, by the end of the lesson.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"smartclass\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, programming software, whiteboard, markers\",\n    \"references\": \"Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book, pages 100-120\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces the concept of pointers in programming, explaining how pointers can be used to manipulate data in a program. Students will learn how to define and use pointers, and will practice using pointers in a programming exercise. The lesson will include a combination of lectures, discussions, and hands-on activities to help students understand the concept of pointers.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized and students participated actively. Most students understood the concept of pointers and were able to use them to manipulate data in a program. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners and provide additional practice exercises to reinforce understanding.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a programmer working on a project that requires you to manipulate large amounts of data. You need to use pointers to efficiently manage the data, but you are not sure how to define and use them.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of how pointers work in programming\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share their prior knowledge of pointers and how they think pointers can be used in programming\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms related to pointers on the board, such as \'pointer\', \'address\', and \'data\'\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the key terms with their definitions\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to provide guidance and answer questions\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a diagram of how pointers work in programming\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to label the different parts of the diagram\",\n            \"Teacher provides a simple example of how pointers can be used in a program\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work individually to complete a short quiz on pointers\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario presented by the teacher\",\n            \"Learners watch the animation video and take notes on how pointers work\",\n            \"Learners share their prior knowledge of pointers and listen to their peers\' responses\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the key terms with their definitions\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners label the different parts of the diagram\",\n            \"Learners work individually to complete the short quiz on pointers\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and ask questions if they are unsure about any concepts\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion to clarify any misconceptions\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned so far and what they need to work on\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to match key terms with their definitions\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and think about how pointers can be used to solve the problem\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how pointers can be used in different programming contexts\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners think about how pointers can be used to efficiently manage data and reduce waste\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners learn about the importance of collaboration and respect in programming\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with exercises on defining and using pointers\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an example of how to use pointers to manipulate data in a program\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to complete the exercises\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to provide guidance and answer questions\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the learners\' work and suggests areas for improvement\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources for learners who need extra support\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work individually to complete a short programming exercise\",\n            \"Teacher provides a rubric for the exercise and explains the expectations\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to submit their work and provides feedback\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete the exercises on defining and using pointers\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Learners work individually to complete the short programming exercise\",\n            \"Learners submit their work and receive feedback from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners review their feedback and make revisions to their work\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion to share their experiences and insights\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they are unsure about\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to complete exercises\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the exercises and think about how to solve the problems\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how pointers can be used in different programming contexts\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            