xperiences and insights\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners participate in a class discussion\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the examples and think about how to apply the concepts\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how pointers can be used in different programming contexts\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners think about how pointers can be used to efficiently manage data and reduce waste\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners learn about the importance of collaboration and respect in programming\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must use pointers to manipulate data in a program\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support as learners work on the project\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the project and suggests areas for improvement\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources for learners who need extra support\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to submit their project and provides feedback\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Teacher provides a rubric for the project and explains the expectations\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to make revisions to their project based on the feedback\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work individually to complete the project\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Learners submit their project and receive feedback from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners review their feedback and make revisions to their project\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion to share their experiences and insights\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they are unsure about\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Learners make revisions to their project based on the feedback\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the project and think about how to apply the concepts\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how pointers can be used in different programming contexts\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners think about how pointers can be used to efficiently manage data and reduce waste\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners learn about the importance of collaboration and respect in programming\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is a pointer in programming? A) A variable that stores a value, B) A variable that stores a memory address, C) A function that returns a value, D) A loop that repeats a statement\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Complete exercises on pages 100-120 in the Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the quiz and suggests areas for improvement\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources for learners who need extra support\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to submit their homework and provides feedback\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Teacher provides a rubric for the homework and explains the expectations\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to make revisions to their homework based on the feedback\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the MCQ quiz: Q1: Expected Answer: B) A variable that stores a memory address\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework and submit it to the teacher\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they are unsure about\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion to share their experiences and insights\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Learners review their feedback and make revisions to their homework\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Learners make revisions to their homework based on the feedback\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to peer-review each other\'s work\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the quiz and think about how to apply the concepts\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how pointers can be used in different programming contexts\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on what they have learned and what they need to work on\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners ask questions and seek guidance from the teacher\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Gender Education - Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Environmental and sustainability - Learners think about how pointers can be used to efficiently manage data and reduce waste\",\n            \"Cross-Cutting Issues: Peace and Values Education - Learners learn about the importance of collaboration and respect in programming\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 3, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 16:03:40', '2026-01-29 16:03:40'),
(20, 6, '```json\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with hearing impairment, 1 student with speech and language difficulties will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Pointer and Structure\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of pointers and structures in programming.\\n. Apply pointers and structures in solving real-world problems.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Dereference and Reference Operators\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and programming software, students with varying learning abilities, under the guidance of the teacher, at the end of this lesson, will be able to identify and use dereference and reference operators correctly in different programming contexts with 80% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, programming software, whiteboard, and markers\",\n    \"references\": \"Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book, pages 100-120\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces students to the concept of dereference and reference operators in programming, focusing on their application in pointers and structures. Through a combination of theoretical explanations, practical exercises, and group discussions, students will gain a comprehensive understanding of how to use these operators effectively. The lesson will begin with an engaging scenario, followed by an exploration of the concepts, explanation of key points, elaboration through real-world examples, and conclude with an evaluation of students\\\' understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured, and students participated actively in the discussions and exercises. Most students demonstrated a good understanding of the concepts, but some struggled with applying the dereference and reference operators in complex scenarios. Next time, I will include more examples and provide additional support for slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a programmer tasked with developing a software that manages a large database of customer information. You need to use pointers and structures to efficiently store and retrieve the data.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to discuss in pairs: What are the benefits of using pointers and structures in programming?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video on the basics of pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Teacher writes a simple program on the board to demonstrate the use of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to identify the operators used in the program and explain their functions.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the key elements: data storage, retrieval, and manipulation.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as pointers, structures, and operators.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the program and the operators used.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the program and the operators.\",\n            \"Learners discuss in pairs the benefits of using pointers and structures in programming.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their ideas.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify the key elements.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussions and activities.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with exercises on using dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they have to write a program using pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of memory allocation and deallocation.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of real-world applications of pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to solve a problem using pointers and structures.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the exercises and solve them.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their findings.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of memory allocation and deallocation.\",\n            \"Learners identify the real-world applications of pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the problem using pointers and structures.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design and implement their own programs using pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their time and resources to complete the exercises and experiment.\",\n            \"Environmental and Sustainability: Learners consider the environmental impact of their programming decisions.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the syntax and semantics of the operators.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the differences between the operators.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of correct and incorrect usage of the operators.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to identify the operators used in a given program.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Learners identify the syntax and semantics of the operators.\",\n            \"Learners understand the differences between the operators.\",\n            \"Learners recognize the correct and incorrect usage of the operators.\",\n            \"Learners identify the operators used in a given program.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long Learning: Learners develop their understanding of the concepts and apply them to new situations.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners consider the financial implications of their programming decisions.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use technology to learn about and apply the concepts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners have to design and implement a program using pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the advantages and disadvantages of using pointers and structures in programming.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the learners\\\' programs and suggests improvements.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to share their programs and experiences with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners design and implement their own programs using pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate and share their opinions.\",\n            \"Learners receive feedback on their programs and implement the suggested improvements.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners share their programs and experiences with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners consider the ethical implications of their programming decisions.\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners are encouraged to participate and share their ideas and experiences.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and evaluate their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz: Q1: What is the purpose of the dereference operator? A) To allocate memory, B) To deallocate memory, C) To access the value of a pointer, D) To change the value of a pointer. Q2: What is the difference between a pointer and a structure? A) A pointer is a variable that holds a memory address, B) A structure is a collection of variables of different data types, C) A pointer is a collection of variables of the same data type, D) A structure is a variable that holds a memory address.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Write a program that uses pointers and structures to store and retrieve data. Q3: What is the syntax of the reference operator? A) &, B) *, C) -, D) +. Q4: What is the purpose of the reference operator? A) To access the value of a pointer, B) To change the value of a pointer, C) To allocate memory, D) To deallocate memory. Q5: What is the advantage of using pointers and structures in programming? A) They improve the efficiency of the program, B) They reduce the complexity of the program, C) They increase the readability of the program, D) They decrease the maintainability of the program.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions: Q1: C) To access the value of a pointer, Q2: B) A structure is a collection of variables of different data types, Q3: A) &, Q4: A) To access the value of a pointer, Q5: A) They improve the efficiency of the program.\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework assignment and submit it to the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their time and resources to complete the quiz and homework.\",\n            \"Life-long Learning: Learners develop their understanding of the concepts and apply them to new situations.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and evaluate their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 4, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 16:41:37', '2026-01-29 16:41:37');
INSERT INTO `lesson_plans` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `content`, `version`, `generated_by_ai`, `ai_provider`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(21, 7, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with Physical disability, 1 with Social, Emotional & Behavioral difficulties will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Unit 6 - Pointer and Structure\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of structures in C++\\n. Apply structures in programming to solve real-world problems\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Structures in C++\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and programming tools, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to define and explain the concept of structures in C++ and apply them in programming to solve real-world problems perfectly.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, C++ compilers, whiteboard, markers\",\n    \"references\": \"Computer Science Senior 5 StudentBook\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces the concept of structures in C++ and their application in programming. Students will learn how to define and use structures to solve real-world problems. The lesson will include engaging activities, exploratory experiments, explanatory discussions, and evaluative assessments to ensure students achieve the learning objectives.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and students participated actively in the activities. Most students understood the concept of structures in C++ and could apply them in programming. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners and provide additional practice exercises to reinforce understanding.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a programmer tasked with creating a system to manage student records. You need to store information such as student names, ages, and grades. How would you approach this problem?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video on the importance of data structures in programming\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm and discuss the benefits of using structures in programming\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms related to structures in C++ on the board, such as \'struct\', \'variables\', and \'functions\'\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share their prior knowledge and experience with programming and data structures\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario presented by the teacher\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video, such as the use of arrays and linked lists\",\n            \"Learners participate in the brainstorming and discussion activity, sharing their ideas and thoughts\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms related to structures in C++\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss and share ideas in pairs and groups\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and think critically about how to approach the problem\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with examples of structures in C++ and asks students to identify and explain the different components\",\n            \"Teacher guides students through an experiment where they create and use a simple structure in C++ to store and manipulate data\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to use functions to manipulate and access data within a structure\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional examples and exercises for students to practice and reinforce their understanding\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to assist and provide feedback to students\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete the worksheet and identify the different components of a structure in C++\",\n            \"Learners participate in the experiment and create their own simple structure in C++\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have about using functions with structures\",\n            \"Learners complete the additional exercises and practice problems to reinforce their understanding\",\n            \"Learners share their work and results with the class and discuss any challenges they faced\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design and create their own structures in C++\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners work independently and manage their time to complete the exercises and experiments\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of structures in C++ and explains the syntax and semantics\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how to use structures in programming to solve real-world problems\",\n            \"Teacher explains the benefits and advantages of using structures in programming, such as improved code organization and reusability\",\n            \"Teacher discusses common pitfalls and errors to avoid when working with structures in C++\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources and references for students to learn more about structures in C++\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of structures in C++ and the syntax and semantics\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the benefits and advantages of using structures in programming\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have about using structures in C++\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete a quiz on the concept of structures in C++\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners understand the importance of efficient programming and data structures in real-world applications\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must create a simple database using structures in C++\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidelines and requirements for the project, including the use of functions and data validation\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to be creative and think critically about how to design and implement the database\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources and references for learners to learn more about database design and implementation\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to assist and provide feedback to learners\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design and implement the database using structures in C++\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the challenges and benefits of using structures in database design and implementation\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have about the project\",\n            \"Learners complete the project and present their results to the class\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners work in groups and respect each other\'s ideas and contributions\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners are encouraged to participate and contribute to the project, regardless of their abilities or backgrounds\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz on the concept of structures in C++: \\n1. What is the purpose of using structures in programming? \\nA) To improve code readability \\nB) To increase program efficiency \\nC) To reduce memory usage \\nD) To simplify data manipulation \\n2. What is the syntax for declaring a structure in C++? \\nA) struct name { variables; } \\nB) struct name ( variables; ) \\nC) struct name { variables } \\nD) struct name ( variables ) \\n3. What is the benefit of using functions with structures in C++? \\nA) Improved code organization \\nB) Increased program efficiency \\nC) Reduced memory usage \\nD) Simplified data manipulation \\n4. What is the common pitfall to avoid when working with structures in C++? \\nA) Using incorrect syntax \\nB) Forgetting to initialize variables \\nC) Not validating user input \\nD) All of the above \\n5. What is the importance of using structures in programming? \\nA) To improve code readability \\nB) To increase program efficiency \\nC) To reduce memory usage \\nD) To simplify data manipulation\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Complete exercises 1-5 on page 123 of the textbook and create a simple program using structures in C++ to solve a real-world problem\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners on their performance and progress\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have\",\n            \"Teacher reflects on the lesson and identifies areas for improvement\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions and submit their answers to the teacher\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework and submit their work to the teacher\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have about the quiz or homework\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to the teacher on the lesson and suggest areas for improvement\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Gender Education: Learners are encouraged to participate and contribute to the lesson, regardless of their gender\",\n            \"Environmental and Sustainability Education: Learners understand the importance of efficient programming and data structures in reducing energy consumption and environmental impact\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 16:47:21', '2026-01-29 16:47:21'),
(22, 6, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"2 students with hearing impairment, 1 student with speech and language difficulties will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Unit 6 - Pointer and Structure\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of pointers and structures in programming.\\n. Apply pointers and structures to solve real-world problems.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Dereference and Reference Operators\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and programming software, every student in the class will be able to identify and explain the use of dereference and reference operators in programming, given a set of examples and exercises, with at least 80% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, programming software, whiteboard, markers\",\n    \"references\": \"Computer Science Senior 5 Student Book, pages 120-125\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce the concepts of dereference and reference operators in programming, and how they are used to access and manipulate data. Students will learn through a combination of lectures, discussions, and hands-on exercises. The lesson will start with an introduction to the topic, followed by a detailed explanation of the concepts, and then students will work on exercises to practice their understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured and students participated actively in the discussions and exercises. Most students understood the concepts of dereference and reference operators, but some struggled with applying them to solve problems. Next time, I will provide more examples and exercises to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a programmer working on a project that requires you to access and manipulate data stored in a complex data structure. How would you use pointers and structures to achieve this?\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share their thoughts and ideas on how they would approach this problem.\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms and concepts related to pointers and structures on the board, such as \'dereference\' and \'reference operators\'.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a brief overview of the lesson objectives and outcomes.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to consider how they can apply their prior knowledge of programming to learn about pointers and structures.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario presented by the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners share their thoughts and ideas on how they would approach the problem.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on key terms and concepts related to pointers and structures.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners begin to think about how they can apply their prior knowledge of programming to learn about pointers and structures.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss and share their thoughts and ideas with each other.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think critically about how they would approach the problem presented in the scenario.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a guided example of how to use dereference and reference operators in programming, using a simple code snippet.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the syntax and semantics of dereference and reference operators, using visual aids such as diagrams and flowcharts.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of exercises for students to practice using dereference and reference operators, with varying levels of difficulty.\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to provide support and guidance to students as they work on the exercises.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and encouragement to students as they complete the exercises.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work on the exercises provided by the teacher, using dereference and reference operators to solve problems.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners share their solutions with each other and discuss any challenges they faced.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Learners begin to think about how they can apply dereference and reference operators to real-world problems.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to apply dereference and reference operators to solve problems.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a detailed explanation of the concepts of dereference and reference operators, using real-world examples and analogies.\",\n            \"Teacher uses visual aids such as diagrams and flowcharts to illustrate the concepts.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of examples and non-examples to help students understand the concepts.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to provide their own examples and non-examples of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and encouragement to students as they provide their examples and non-examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concepts of dereference and reference operators, using their own words and examples.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners share their notes with each other and discuss any challenges they faced.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Learners begin to think about how they can apply dereference and reference operators to real-world problems.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think critically about the concepts of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners recognize the importance of ongoing learning and professional development in the field of programming.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project that requires students to apply dereference and reference operators to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support to students as they work on the project.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to think creatively and come up with innovative solutions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and encouragement to students as they work on the project.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to present their projects to the class and provide feedback to each other.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work on the project, applying dereference and reference operators to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners share their projects with each other and discuss any challenges they faced.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Learners begin to think about how they can apply dereference and reference operators to other real-world problems.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to apply dereference and reference operators to solve real-world problems.\",\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work together and share their ideas and solutions with each other.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a quiz with 5 multiple-choice questions to assess students\' understanding of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to complete the quiz and then review the answers as a class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and encouragement to students based on their performance on the quiz.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework that requires students to apply dereference and reference operators to solve problems.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners complete the quiz and then review the answers as a class.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\",\n            \"Learners begin to think about how they can apply dereference and reference operators to other real-world problems.\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework assignment and submit it to the teacher for feedback.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think critically about the concepts of dereference and reference operators.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their own learning and identify areas where they need more practice or review.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 5, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 16:49:55', '2026-01-29 16:49:55'),
(23, 1, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"No students with special needs are identified in this class. However, the teacher will ensure that all learners are supported through the use of various teaching methods and materials.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Introduction To Quadratic Equation\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of quadratic equations and their applications.\\n. Solve quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Introduction to quadratic equations\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using various mathematical tools and techniques, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to define and explain the concept of quadratic equations and their applications perfectly, given the condition of having prior knowledge of linear equations and algebraic expressions, with a degree of accuracy of at least 80%.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"smartclass\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Whiteboard, markers, quadratic equation worksheets, calculators\",\n    \"references\": \"Mathematics textbook, Chapter 5: Quadratic Equations\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces the concept of quadratic equations, their definition, and applications. Learners will engage in activities to understand the concept, explore different methods of solving quadratic equations, and evaluate their understanding through quizzes and exercises. The lesson will be conducted in a smartclass with the use of various mathematical tools and techniques.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concept of quadratic equations and their applications. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners and provide additional practice exercises to reinforce understanding.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A farmer has 100 meters of fencing and wants to enclose a rectangular area. If the length of the area is x meters, find the width in terms of x.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to discuss in pairs: What are the possible values of x? What are the implications of different values of x on the width?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a video on real-world applications of quadratic equations, such as projectile motion and electrical circuits.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to brainstorm: What are some other real-world applications of quadratic equations?\",\n            \"Teacher writes on the board: ax² + bx + c = 0, and asks learners to identify the different parts of the equation.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a puzzle related to quadratic equations and asks learners to solve it.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Teacher uses a calculator to demonstrate the solution of a simple quadratic equation.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to match different quadratic equations with their corresponding graphs.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a quiz with 5 multiple-choice questions to assess learners\' prior knowledge of quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the variables and the relationships between them.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video, such as the equation of motion and the role of gravity.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition and applications of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the puzzle and present their solutions to the class.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use calculators to solve simple quadratic equations and check their answers.\",\n            \"Learners match different quadratic equations with their corresponding graphs and discuss any patterns or observations.\",\n            \"Learners complete the quiz and review their answers with the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their prior knowledge of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify the variables and relationships between them.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use calculators to solve simple quadratic equations and explore their graphs.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with exercises on solving quadratic equations using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they measure the height of a projectile and calculate its trajectory using quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates the use of graphing calculators to visualize quadratic equations and identify their roots.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to solve a set of quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of word problems that involve quadratic equations, such as optimizing the area of a rectangle.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to use technology, such as computer algebra systems, to solve and visualize quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Teacher writes on the board: x² + 4x + 4 = 0, and asks learners to factor the equation.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of quadratic equations with different coefficients and asks learners to identify the patterns and relationships between them.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to create their own word problems that involve quadratic equations and share them with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the exercises and experiments.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the exercises and solve the quadratic equations using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment and record their results, then calculate the trajectory of the projectile using quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use graphing calculators to visualize quadratic equations and identify their roots.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the set of quadratic equations using different methods and present their solutions to the class.\",\n            \"Learners solve the word problems and optimize the area of the rectangle using quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use technology to solve and visualize quadratic equations, and explore their properties and applications.\",\n            \"Learners factor the equation x² + 4x + 4 = 0 and identify the roots.\",\n            \"Learners identify the patterns and relationships between the quadratic equations with different coefficients.\",\n            \"Learners create their own word problems that involve quadratic equations and share them with the class.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the exercises and solve the quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners create their own word problems that involve quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of quadratic equations as ax² + bx + c = 0, and explains the different methods of solving them.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula: x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / 2a, and explains the derivation and application of the formula.\",\n            \"Teacher writes on the board: x² + 5x + 6 = 0, and asks learners to solve the equation using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates the use of graphing calculators to visualize quadratic equations and identify their roots.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of discriminant and its role in determining the nature of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of real-world applications of quadratic equations, such as optimizing the area of a rectangle.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to solve a set of quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the exercises and experiments.\",\n            \"Teacher writes on the board: x² - 4x - 3 = 0, and asks learners to solve the equation using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition and applications of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to solve the equation x² + 5x + 6 = 0, and check their answers using graphing calculators.\",\n            \"Learners solve the equation x² - 4x - 3 = 0 using factoring and the quadratic formula, and identify the roots.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the set of quadratic equations using different methods and present their solutions to the class.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use graphing calculators to visualize quadratic equations and identify their roots.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners create their own examples of real-world applications of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners solve the equation x² + 2x - 6 = 0 using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Learners identify the patterns and relationships between the quadratic equations with different coefficients.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to solve the set of quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the exercises and solve the quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must create a real-world application of quadratic equations, such as optimizing the area of a rectangle.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of quadratic equations on real-world problems, such as predicting population growth.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of word problems that involve quadratic equations, such as calculating the trajectory of a projectile.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to use technology, such as computer algebra systems, to solve and visualize quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to solve a set of quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the project and debate.\",\n            \"Teacher writes on the board: x² + 3x - 2 = 0, and asks learners to solve the equation using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of quadratic equations with different coefficients and asks learners to identify the patterns and relationships between them.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to create their own word problems that involve quadratic equations and share them with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a real-world application of quadratic equations, such as optimizing the area of a rectangle.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate and discuss the impact of quadratic equations on real-world problems.\",\n            \"Learners solve the word problems and calculate the trajectory of the projectile using quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use technology to solve and visualize quadratic equations, and explore their properties and applications.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the set of quadratic equations using different methods and present their solutions to the class.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners create their own examples of real-world applications of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners solve the equation x² - 2x - 3 = 0 using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Learners identify the patterns and relationships between the quadratic equations with different coefficients.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners create their own real-world applications of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners consider the environmental impact of their real-world applications of quadratic equations.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz: Q1: What is the formula for solving quadratic equations? A) x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / 2a, B) x = (-b ± √(b² + 4ac)) / 2a, C) x = (-b ± √(b² - 2ac)) / 2a, D) x = (-b ± √(b² + 2ac)) / 2a. Q2: What is the discriminant of the quadratic equation x² + 4x + 4 = 0? A) 0, B) 4, C) 8, D) 16. Q3: What is the solution to the quadratic equation x² - 4x - 3 = 0? A) x = -1 or x = 3, B) x = 1 or x = -3, C) x = 2 or x = -2, D) x = 3 or x = -1. Q4: What is the graph of the quadratic equation x² + 2x - 6 = 0? A) A parabola that opens upwards, B) A parabola that opens downwards, C) A straight line, D) A circle. Q5: What is the real-world application of quadratic equations? A) Optimizing the area of a rectangle, B) Predicting population growth, C) Calculating the trajectory of a projectile, D) All of the above.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve problems 1-5 on the worksheet, which include solving quadratic equations using factoring and the quadratic formula, and identifying the patterns and relationships between quadratic equations with different coefficients.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they complete the quiz and homework.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Teacher writes on the board: x² + x - 2 = 0, and asks learners to solve the equation using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of quadratic equations with different coefficients and asks learners to identify the patterns and relationships between them.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to create their own word problems that involve quadratic equations and share them with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to use technology, such as computer algebra systems, to solve and visualize quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A) x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / 2a, Q2: Expected Answer: A) 0, Q3: Expected Answer: A) x = -1 or x = 3, Q4: Expected Answer: A) A parabola that opens upwards, Q5: Expected Answer: D) All of the above.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions if they need clarification.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and share their thoughts on the concept of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use technology to solve and visualize quadratic equations, and explore their properties and applications.\",\n            \"Learners solve the equation x² + x - 2 = 0 using factoring and the quadratic formula.\",\n            \"Learners identify the patterns and relationships between the quadratic equations with different coefficients.\",\n            \"Learners create their own word problems that involve quadratic equations and share them with the class.\",\n            \"Learners use graphing calculators to visualize quadratic equations and identify their roots.\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion to review the key concepts and applications of quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the exercises and solve the quadratic equations using different methods.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their understanding of quadratic equations and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners consider the financial implications of their real-world applications of quadratic equations.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 16:51:17', '2026-01-29 16:51:17');
INSERT INTO `lesson_plans` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `content`, `version`, `generated_by_ai`, `ai_provider`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(24, 8, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"No students with special needs are identified. However, if there were students with special needs, these students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Vectors in 2D\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and explain the concept of vectors in 2D space.\\n. Apply vector operations such as addition and scalar multiplication.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Introduction to vectors in 2D\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using visual aids and real-world examples, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to define and identify vectors in 2D space, and explain their importance with 90% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"inside\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Whiteboard, markers, ruler, graph paper, calculator\",\n    \"references\": \"Mathematics S4 SB\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces the concept of vectors in 2D space, covering definition, notation, and basic operations. Students will engage with real-world scenarios, explore vector properties, and apply their understanding through calculations and graphing. The lesson concludes with an evaluation of student understanding through quizzes and class discussion.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concept of vectors. Next time, I will include more visual aids and real-world examples to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A boat is sailing across a lake with a velocity of 5 m/s. The wind is blowing at 3 m/s. How can we represent the boat\'s motion using vectors?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a car moving on a grid, demonstrating how vectors can be used to describe motion.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to share examples of how vectors are used in real-life situations.\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms related to vectors on the board, such as magnitude, direction, and scalar multiplication.\",\n            \"Teacher distributes a handout with a diagram of a vector in 2D space and asks learners to identify its components.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the vectors involved and how they interact.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video, such as the car\'s velocity and direction.\",\n            \"Learners share their own examples of vectors in real-life situations, such as throwing a ball or kicking a soccer ball.\",\n            \"Learners copy down the key terms and their definitions in their notebooks.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to identify the components of the vector in the handout diagram.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their thoughts with the class.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify the vectors involved.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with exercises on adding and subtracting vectors in 2D space.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they measure the magnitude and direction of vectors using a ruler and protractor.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to calculate the resultant vector when two vectors are added together.\",\n            \"Teacher distributes a graph paper and asks learners to plot vectors and calculate their magnitudes and directions.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of scalar multiplication and its effect on vector magnitude and direction.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the exercises to find the resultant vector when two vectors are added together.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their measurements in a table.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to calculate the resultant vector and compare their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Learners plot vectors on the graph paper and calculate their magnitudes and directions using the Pythagorean theorem.\",\n            \"Learners apply scalar multiplication to vectors and observe how it affects their magnitude and direction.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design and conduct their own experiments to measure vector magnitude and direction.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners work independently to complete exercises and plot vectors on graph paper.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of vector addition and subtraction using diagrams and equations.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for calculating the magnitude of a vector: |vector| = √(x² + y²).\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of vector notation, including the use of arrows and coordinates.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to calculate the direction of a vector using trigonometry.\",\n            \"Teacher summarizes the key points of the lesson on the board, including vector definition, notation, and operations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition and notation of vectors, including the use of arrows and coordinates.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to calculate the magnitude of a vector and check their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to calculate the direction of a vector using trigonometry and compare their answers.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions to clarify any doubts about vector concepts and operations.\",\n            \"Learners copy down the summary of key points in their notebooks.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners recognize the importance of vectors in real-life situations and their application in various fields.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners understand the economic implications of vector calculations in fields such as physics and engineering.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design and conduct an experiment to measure the velocity of a rolling ball using vectors.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the importance of vectors in real-life situations, such as navigation and engineering.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a case study of a real-world problem that involves vector calculations, such as designing a bridge or a building.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to research and present on a topic related to vectors, such as their application in computer graphics or video games.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to think critically about the limitations and potential biases of vector calculations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design and conduct the experiment, measuring the velocity of the rolling ball using vectors.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate, presenting their arguments for or against the importance of vectors in real-life situations.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and calculate the vectors involved in the problem, presenting their solutions to the class.\",\n            \"Learners research and present on their chosen topic, applying vector concepts and calculations to real-world problems.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on the limitations and potential biases of vector calculations and discuss ways to address these issues.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners consider the environmental impact of vector calculations in fields such as engineering and architecture.\",\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners recognize the importance of vectors in promoting peace and stability in fields such as navigation and international relations.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question quiz on vectors in 2D space, including multiple-choice and short-answer questions.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Calculate the magnitude and direction of a vector given its components, and plot the vector on graph paper.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they learned during the lesson and what they would like to learn more about in the future.\",\n            \"Teacher distributes a feedback form for learners to evaluate the lesson and provide suggestions for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher summarizes the key points of the lesson and provides additional resources for further learning.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions, including: 1. What is the definition of a vector? A) A scalar quantity, B) A vector quantity, C) A unit vector, D) A zero vector. Expected answer: B) A vector quantity.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions to clarify any doubts about the assignment.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and write down what they would like to learn more about in the future.\",\n            \"Learners complete the feedback form, providing suggestions for improvement and evaluating the lesson.\",\n            \"Learners review the summary of key points and ask questions to clarify any doubts.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners recognize the importance of vectors in promoting inclusivity and accessibility in fields such as architecture and engineering.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners apply vector calculations using digital tools, such as graphing calculators and computer software.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 16:54:58', '2026-01-29 16:54:58'),
(25, 9, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with physical disability will be helped by using a wheelchair ramp to access the classroom and providing extra support during experiments. These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"GERMINATION\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different types of germination and explain their characteristics.\\n. Apply concepts of germination in real-life scenarios.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Types of Germination\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using diagrams and illustrations, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and describe the different types of germination perfectly, under normal classroom conditions, with at least 80% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"diagrams, illustrations, seeds, soil, water\",\n    \"references\": \"Science and Elementary Technology textbook, chapter 9\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to the concept of germination, its importance, and the different types of germination. Students will engage in hands-on activities to explore and understand the process of germination. The lesson will conclude with an evaluation of students\\\' understanding through a quiz and homework assignment.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured and students participated actively in the experiments. Most students understood the concepts of germination. Next time, I will include more visual aids and provide extra support to students with special needs.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a farmer and you want to grow crops, but you don\\\'t know how seeds germinate. What would you do to learn about germination?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a seed germinating and asks students to observe and describe the process.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm and discuss the importance of germination in everyday life.\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms related to germination on the board, such as \\\"seed\\\", \\\"soil\\\", \\\"water\\\", and \\\"light\\\".\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share their prior knowledge about germination and what they would like to learn.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by sharing their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video, such as the seed, soil, water, and light.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the brainstorming and discussion, sharing their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Learners copy down the key terms related to germination and ask questions for clarification.\",\n            \"Learners share their prior knowledge and what they would like to learn about germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and video to understand the process of germination.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with diagrams of different types of seeds and asks students to identify and label the parts.\",\n            \"Teacher guides students through an experiment where they plant seeds in soil and observe the germination process.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the importance of water, light, and temperature in the germination process.\",\n            \"Teacher provides students with a handout on the different types of germination, including epigeal and hypogeal germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the types of germination with their characteristics.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the diagrams and label the parts of the seeds.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the experiment and observe the germination process.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the importance of water, light, and temperature in the germination process.\",\n            \"Learners read the handout on the different types of germination and ask questions for clarification.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the types of germination with their characteristics and discuss any challenges they encounter.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design and conduct an experiment to observe the germination process.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning and work in pairs to complete the matching activity.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of epigeal germination and explains its characteristics.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for calculating the percentage of germination: (number of seeds germinated / total number of seeds) x 100.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the advantages and disadvantages of epigeal and hypogeal germination.\",\n            \"Teacher uses diagrams to illustrate the process of germination and asks students to follow along.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to provide examples of plants that exhibit epigeal and hypogeal germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of epigeal germination and its characteristics.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to calculate the percentage of germination and ask questions for clarification.\",\n            \"Learners discuss the advantages and disadvantages of epigeal and hypogeal germination in small groups.\",\n            \"Learners follow along with the diagrams and ask questions to clarify their understanding.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of plants that exhibit epigeal and hypogeal germination and discuss any challenges they encounter.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners apply the formula to calculate the percentage of germination and discuss the results.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners discuss the economic importance of germination in agriculture and horticulture.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design and conduct an experiment to compare the effects of different environmental factors on germination.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of climate change on germination and plant growth.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to research and present on the different types of seeds and their germination requirements.\",\n            \"Teacher provides students with a case study on a real-world scenario where germination is critical, such as in agriculture or conservation.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in groups to design a plan for a community garden, taking into account the different types of germination and environmental factors.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design and conduct the experiment, collecting and analyzing data.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate, presenting their arguments and listening to others.\",\n            \"Learners research and present on the different types of seeds and their germination requirements, using visual aids and handouts.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and discuss the implications of germination in real-world scenarios.\",\n            \"Learners work in groups to design the plan for the community garden, taking into account the different types of germination and environmental factors.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners discuss the impact of climate change on germination and plant growth.\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners work in groups to design a plan for a community garden, taking into account the needs of all members.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is the primary factor that affects germination? A) Water, B) Light, C) Temperature, D) Soil. Q2: Which type of germination is characterized by the seedling emerging from the soil? A) Epigeal, B) Hypogeal, C) Both, D) Neither.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve problems 1-5 on the worksheet, which include calculating the percentage of germination and identifying the characteristics of epigeal and hypogeal germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on what they learned and what they would like to learn more about.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their participation and engagement during the lesson.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to provide feedback on the lesson and suggest improvements.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A) Water, Q2: Expected Answer: A) Epigeal.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions for clarification.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they learned and what they would like to learn more about, writing down their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Learners receive feedback from the teacher and ask questions to clarify their understanding.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback on the lesson and suggest improvements, using a feedback form or writing down their thoughts and ideas.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners reflect on what they learned and what they would like to learn more about, considering the values of respect and responsibility.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use digital tools to complete the homework assignment and provide feedback on the lesson.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 18:19:22', '2026-01-29 18:19:22'),
(26, 9, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with physical disability will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"GERMINATION\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Types of Germination\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different types of germination perfectly.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"computers, telephones, radio, animation video, seeds, soil, water\",\n    \"references\": \"Science and Elementary Technology textbook, chapter 5\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to the concept of germination, including the different types of germination. Students will explore the process of germination through hands-on experiments and multimedia presentations. The lesson will conclude with a quiz to assess students\' understanding of the topic.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was organized and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a farmer and you want to grow crops, but you don\'t know how to make the seeds germinate. What would you do?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a seed germinating and asks students to observe and describe the process.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm and discuss the following questions: What is germination? What are the different types of germination?\",\n            \"Teacher writes the questions on the board and asks students to share their answers.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a brief introduction to the topic of germination and its importance in agriculture.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share any personal experiences they have with germination or planting seeds.\",\n            \"Teacher distributes a handout with a diagram of a seed and asks students to label the different parts.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of vocabulary words related to germination and asks students to define them.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a concept map of the different types of germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by sharing their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as the seed, soil, water, and sunlight.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the brainstorming and discussion activity and share their answers to the questions.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the introduction to the topic and the importance of germination.\",\n            \"Learners share their personal experiences and listen to their peers\' experiences.\",\n            \"Learners label the different parts of the seed and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions and ask for help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners define the vocabulary words and use them in sentences.\",\n            \"Learners create a concept map of the different types of germination and present it to the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify the key elements.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners consider the role of gender in agriculture and germination.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about the different types of germination and asks students to solve it.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they plant seeds in different conditions to observe the effects on germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to observe and record the results of the experiment and discuss the findings.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of guided questions to help students analyze the data and draw conclusions.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a graph to illustrate the results of the experiment.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of materials for students to design and conduct their own experiment on germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in groups to research and present on a specific type of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of resources for students to learn about the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a model of a seed germinating and explain the process.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of case studies for students to analyze and discuss the different types of germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the puzzle and solve it to understand the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment and record the results to analyze the effects of different conditions on germination.\",\n            \"Learners discuss the findings and draw conclusions about the experiment.\",\n            \"Learners create a graph to illustrate the results of the experiment and present it to the class.\",\n            \"Learners design and conduct their own experiment on germination and present the results.\",\n            \"Learners work in groups to research and present on a specific type of germination.\",\n            \"Learners use the resources to learn about the different types of germination and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners create a model of a seed germinating and explain the process to the class.\",\n            \"Learners analyze and discuss the case studies to understand the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the data and draw conclusions.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design and conduct their own experiment on germination.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners consider the impact of germination on the environment.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of germination and explains the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the definition of germination and explains the process.\",\n            \"Teacher uses diagrams and illustrations to explain the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of each type of germination and asks students to identify them.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of guided questions to help students understand the concept of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a concept map of the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of resources for students to learn about the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their understanding of the concept of germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition and process of germination.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different types of germination and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions.\",\n            \"Learners create a concept map of the different types of germination and present it to the class.\",\n            \"Learners use the resources to learn about the different types of germination and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners create a diagram to illustrate the process of germination.\",\n            \"Learners write a short essay on the importance of germination in agriculture.\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the different types of germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners consider the economic importance of germination in agriculture.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design and create a model of a seed germinating.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in groups to research and present on a specific type of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of materials for students to design and conduct their own experiment on germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a graph to illustrate the results of the experiment.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of resources for students to learn about the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their understanding of the concept of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a diagram to illustrate the process of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of case studies for students to analyze and discuss the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to participate in a class discussion on the different types of germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners design and create a model of a seed germinating and present it to the class.\",\n            \"Learners work in groups to research and present on a specific type of germination.\",\n            \"Learners use the materials to design and conduct their own experiment on germination.\",\n            \"Learners create a graph to illustrate the results of the experiment and present it to the class.\",\n            \"Learners use the resources to learn about the different types of germination and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners create a diagram to illustrate the process of germination.\",\n            \"Learners analyze and discuss the case studies to understand the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the different types of germination.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design and create a model of a seed germinating.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and discuss the case studies.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz: Q1: What is germination? A) The process of a seed growing into a plant, B) The process of a plant growing into a seed, C) The process of a seed dying, D) The process of a plant dying. Q2: What are the different types of germination? A) Epigeal and hypogeal, B) Monocot and dicot, C) Annual and perennial, D) Biennial and triennial. Q3: What is the importance of germination in agriculture? A) It allows for the growth of new plants, B) It allows for the production of seeds, C) It allows for the growth of existing plants, D) It allows for the death of plants. Q4: What are the factors that affect germination? A) Temperature, light, and water, B) Temperature, light, and soil, C) Temperature, water, and soil, D) Light, water, and soil. Q5: What is the role of germination in the life cycle of a plant? A) It is the beginning of the life cycle, B) It is the end of the life cycle, C) It is the middle of the life cycle, D) It is not part of the life cycle.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Write a short essay on the importance of germination in agriculture. Answer the following questions: 1. What is germination? 2. What are the different types of germination? 3. What is the importance of germination in agriculture? 4. What are the factors that affect germination? 5. What is the role of germination in the life cycle of a plant?\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their understanding of the concept of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of resources for students to learn about the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to create a diagram to illustrate the process of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of case studies for students to analyze and discuss the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to participate in a class discussion on the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of guided questions to help students understand the concept of germination.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions and submit their answers.\",\n            \"Learners write the short essay on the importance of germination in agriculture and answer the questions.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek feedback from the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners create a diagram to illustrate the process of germination.\",\n            \"Learners analyze and discuss the case studies to understand the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the different types of germination.\",\n            \"Learners use the resources to learn about the different types of germination and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the different types of germination with their definitions.\",\n            \"Learners create a concept map of the different types of germination and present it to the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and discuss the case studies.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their own learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use digital tools to create a diagram to illustrate the process of germination.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 2, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-29 18:19:25', '2026-01-29 18:19:25');
INSERT INTO `lesson_plans` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `content`, `version`, `generated_by_ai`, `ai_provider`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(27, 10, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"No students with special needs are identified in this class. However, if any student needs help, these students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Introduction To Quadratic Equation\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and solve quadratic equations in the form ax^2 + bx + c = 0.\\n. Apply quadratic equations to solve real-world problems.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Quadratic inequalities\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, calculators, and graph paper, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to define, solve, and graph quadratic inequalities with a high degree of accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"inside\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, calculators, graph paper, and whiteboard markers\",\n    \"references\": \"Mathematics Senior 4 Student\'s Book\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to quadratic inequalities, focusing on defining, solving, and graphing these inequalities. Students will engage with real-world scenarios, explore and explain concepts through guided practice, and elaborate on their understanding through group work and presentations. The lesson will conclude with an evaluation of student understanding through quizzes and homework assignments.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts of quadratic inequalities. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners and provide additional visual aids to enhance understanding.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A farmer has 100 meters of fencing to enclose a rectangular area. If the farmer wants to maximize the area, what should be the dimensions of the rectangle?\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm and discuss possible solutions in pairs.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a farmer trying to enclose a rectangular area with fencing.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a class discussion on the importance of maximizing area in real-world applications.\",\n            \"Teacher introduces the concept of quadratic inequalities as a tool to solve this problem.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario in pairs, considering the constraints and possible solutions.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video, such as the length of the fencing and the goal of maximizing the area.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the class discussion, sharing their thoughts on the importance of maximizing area in real-world applications.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the introduction of quadratic inequalities and their relevance to the problem.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on the concept of quadratic inequalities.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and participate in a class discussion.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify key elements.\",\n            \"Gender Education: The scenario is neutral and inclusive, allowing all learners to participate.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with examples of quadratic inequalities, such as x^2 + 4x + 4 > 0.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through solving these inequalities using factoring and graphing.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of the sign chart and how to use it to solve quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to graph quadratic inequalities on a coordinate plane.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a guided practice session, where learners work in pairs to solve quadratic inequalities.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the examples of quadratic inequalities, using factoring and graphing.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the guided practice session, asking questions and seeking clarification.\",\n            \"Learners create their own sign charts to solve quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Learners graph quadratic inequalities on a coordinate plane, using graph paper and colored pencils.\",\n            \"Learners present their solutions to the class, explaining their reasoning and methodology.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners create their own sign charts and graph quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Environmental and Sustainability Education: The use of graph paper and colored pencils promotes sustainability.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of quadratic inequalities, using the example x^2 + 4x + 4 > 0.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for solving quadratic inequalities, such as (x + 2)^2 > 0.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to solve quadratic inequalities using the formula.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the importance of checking the solution set and verifying the inequality.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a class discussion on the different methods for solving quadratic inequalities.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the explanation of quadratic inequalities and the formula for solving them.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the class discussion, asking questions and sharing their thoughts.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to practice solving quadratic inequalities using the formula.\",\n            \"Learners check their solution sets and verify the inequality, using graph paper and calculators.\",\n            \"Learners present their solutions to the class, explaining their reasoning and methodology.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners participate in a class discussion and work in pairs.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, practicing and checking their solutions.\",\n            \"Financial Education: The use of calculators promotes financial literacy and responsibility.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must create a real-world scenario involving quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the importance of quadratic inequalities in real-world applications.\",\n            \"Teacher provides resources and guidance for learners to research and create their projects.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to use technology, such as graphing calculators and computer software, to create their projects.\",\n            \"Teacher allows learners to present their projects to the class, providing feedback and guidance.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to create their real-world scenarios, using quadratic inequalities to solve problems.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate, sharing their thoughts and opinions on the importance of quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Learners research and create their projects, using technology and resources provided by the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners present their projects to the class, explaining their reasoning and methodology.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback and guidance to their peers, promoting a collaborative learning environment.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners create their own real-world scenarios and projects.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve quadratic inequalities in real-world contexts.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners develop skills and knowledge that can be applied in real-world contexts, promoting life-long learning.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz on quadratic inequalities, with questions such as: What is the solution set to the inequality x^2 + 4x + 4 > 0? A) x > -2, B) x < -2, C) x > 0, D) x < 0\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Solve the inequality x^2 - 4x + 4 > 0 and graph the solution set on a coordinate plane.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the expected answers and solutions to the quiz and homework, providing feedback and guidance.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a class discussion on the importance of quadratic inequalities and their real-world applications.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional resources and support for learners who need extra help.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions, using their knowledge and understanding of quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Learners solve the inequality and graph the solution set, using graph paper and colored pencils.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the class discussion, sharing their thoughts and opinions on the importance of quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts or topics they are struggling with.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their own learning, identifying areas of strength and weakness.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze and solve quadratic inequalities.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning, reflecting on their strengths and weaknesses.\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: The quiz and homework assignments are inclusive and accessible, allowing all learners to participate and demonstrate their understanding.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 11:38:44', '2026-01-30 11:38:44'),
(28, 11, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with Physical disability. These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"TIME\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"10.1. Reading and telling the time accurately on digital and analogue watches\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different time-telling tools perfectly.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"Classroom\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Whiteboard, markers, digital watches, analogue watches, computers, telephones, radio, animation video\",\n    \"references\": \"Mathematics P4 Student Book, Mathematics Teachers Guide, Mathematics Student P4 Book Updated Book\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to the concept of time-telling using both digital and analogue watches. The teacher will use various teaching aids such as computers, telephones, radio, and animation video to engage students. The lesson will be divided into three main sections: introduction, development, and conclusion. In the introduction, the teacher will introduce the concept of time-telling and its importance. In the development section, the teacher will explain the different types of time-telling tools and how to use them. In the conclusion, the teacher will assess students\\u2019 understanding of the concept.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was organized and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are going to school and you need to catch the bus at 7:00 am. How will you know what time it is?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video on the importance of time-telling\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share their experiences with time-telling\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms related to time-telling on the board\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to repeat the key terms and explain their meanings\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by sharing their own experiences\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as the clock and the bus\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the importance of time-telling\",\n            \"Learners repeat the key terms and explain their meanings\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about time-telling and its importance\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their experiences\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think critically about the importance of time-telling\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with pictures of digital and analogue watches\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they have to tell the time using both digital and analogue watches\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of time zones and how it affects time-telling\",\n            \"Teacher uses computers and telephones to demonstrate how to set the time\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of real-life situations where time-telling is crucial\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the pictures of digital and analogue watches and identify the hour and minute hands\",\n            \"Learners participate in the experiment and practice telling the time using both digital and analogue watches\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about time zones and how it affects time-telling\",\n            \"Learners use computers and telephones to practice setting the time\",\n            \"Learners discuss in groups the importance of time-telling in real-life situations\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to tell the time using different tools\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners practice setting the time and managing their time effectively\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of time-telling and explains the difference between digital and analogue watches\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for calculating the time: hour + minute = time\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of half past, quarter to, and quarter past\",\n            \"Teacher uses visual aids to demonstrate how to tell the time\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how to apply the concept of time-telling in real-life situations\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition of time-telling and the difference between digital and analogue watches\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to calculate the time\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about half past, quarter to, and quarter past\",\n            \"Learners use visual aids to practice telling the time\",\n            \"Learners discuss in groups how to apply the concept of time-telling in real-life situations\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners learn about the concept of time-telling and its importance\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners learn about the importance of time-telling in managing time and resources effectively\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners have to create their own analogue watch\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the importance of time-telling in modern society\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how time-telling is used in different professions\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to research and present on the history of time-telling\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on learners\\u2019 projects and presentations\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design and create their own analogue watch\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate and discuss the importance of time-telling\",\n            \"Learners research and present on the history of time-telling\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and provide feedback on their peers\\u2019 projects and presentations\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it in real-life situations\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think critically about the importance of time-telling\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to design and create their own analogue watch\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is the difference between digital and analogue watches? A) Digital watches show the time in numbers, B) Analogue watches show the time in numbers, C) Digital watches show the time in hands, D) Analogue watches show the time in hands. Q2: How do you tell the time on an analogue watch? A) By looking at the hour hand, B) By looking at the minute hand, C) By looking at both the hour and minute hands, D) By looking at the second hand.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Create a schedule for a day using both digital and analogue watches.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on learners\\u2019 quizzes and homework\",\n            \"Teacher summarizes the key points learned in the lesson\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the MCQ quiz: Q1: Expected Answer: A, Q2: Expected Answer: C\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it in real-life situations\",\n            \"Learners participate in a class discussion on the importance of time-telling\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts they have\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use computers and telephones to practice telling the time\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners learn about the importance of time-telling for people with disabilities\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 11:54:41', '2026-01-30 11:54:41'),
(29, 12, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with physical disability. These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"TIME\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different time concepts used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply time concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Writing Time Using Ante Meridian to mean before noon (AM) and Post Meridian to mean after noon (PM)\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using clocks and time-telling strategies, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the time using AM and PM perfectly, given a clock face and a time in standard form.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"smartclass\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"clocks, whiteboard, markers, computers with internet\",\n    \"references\": \"Mathematics P4 Student Book, Mathematics Teachers Guide, Mathematics Student P4 Book Updated Book\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce the concept of time using AM and PM. Students will learn to tell time using clocks and convert between standard time and AM/PM time. The lesson will include interactive activities, group discussions, and hands-on exercises to reinforce understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts of AM and PM. Next time, I will include more visual aids and provide additional practice exercises to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"10 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you have a meeting at 3:00 PM. How would you write this time using AM and PM?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a clock face with 3:00 PM marked and asks students to identify the time.\",\n            \"Teacher writes the time in standard form (15:00) and asks students to convert it to AM/PM time.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share times they have seen or used before, such as 12:00 PM or 6:00 AM.\",\n            \"Teacher introduces the concept of AM (ante meridian) and PM (post meridian) and explains their meanings.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe the clock face and identify the time.\",\n            \"Learners convert the standard time to AM/PM time.\",\n            \"Learners share their own experiences with time-telling.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about AM and PM.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the definitions of AM and PM.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their understanding of time-telling.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners convert between standard time and AM/PM time.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"24 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with clock faces and times marked in standard form.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an exercise where they convert standard times to AM/PM times.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to tell time using a clock face and explains the concept of half-past and quarter-to.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of times in AM and PM, such as 6:00 AM and 12:00 PM.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to match standard times with their AM/PM equivalents.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners complete the worksheets and convert standard times to AM/PM times.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the exercise and ask questions about time-telling.\",\n            \"Learners observe the clock face and practice telling time.\",\n            \"Learners match standard times with their AM/PM equivalents.\",\n            \"Learners discuss any challenges they faced during the exercise.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about time-telling and come up with their own examples.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their time effectively to complete the exercise.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of AM and PM and explains how to use them correctly.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for converting standard time to AM/PM time: if the hour is less than 12, use AM; if the hour is 12 or greater, use PM.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of 12:00 PM (noon) and how it affects time-telling.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of times in AM and PM, such as 3:00 PM and 9:00 AM.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to provide their own examples of times in AM and PM.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definitions and formulas for AM and PM.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to convert standard times to AM/PM times.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the concept of noon and how it affects time-telling.\",\n            \"Learners provide their own examples of times in AM and PM.\",\n            \"Learners discuss any challenges they faced during the explanation.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners recognize the importance of time-telling in their daily lives.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners understand the value of time and how it relates to financial planning.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must create their own clock faces with times marked in AM and PM.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a discussion on the importance of time-telling in real-life situations, such as scheduling appointments or meetings.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how time-telling is used in different professions, such as medicine or transportation.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to research and present on a topic related to time-telling, such as the history of clocks or time zones.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to think critically about the impact of time-telling on their daily lives.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to create their own clock faces with times marked in AM and PM.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the discussion and share their thoughts on the importance of time-telling.\",\n            \"Learners research and present on a topic related to time-telling.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and provide feedback on their peers\' presentations.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it in their daily lives.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Gender Education: Learners recognize the importance of time-telling in different cultural and social contexts.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners understand the impact of time-telling on environmental sustainability, such as energy consumption.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"6 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question quiz: Q1: What does AM stand for? A) After Midnight, B) Ante Meridian, C) After Noon, D) Ante Noon. Q2: What is the time 15:00 in AM/PM format? A) 3:00 PM, B) 3:00 AM, C) 12:00 PM, D) 12:00 AM.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Create a schedule for a day, including times in AM and PM.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it in their daily lives.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the quiz and homework assignments.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions and seek help if needed.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions: Q1: B) Ante Meridian, Q2: A) 3:00 PM.\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework assignment and create a schedule for a day.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they have learned and how they can apply it in their daily lives.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback on the lesson and suggest improvements.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners recognize the importance of time-telling in promoting peace and understanding.\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners understand the importance of accommodating different learning styles and needs in time-telling.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 12:03:11', '2026-01-30 12:03:11'),
(30, 13, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with physical disability, These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"PLANTS GERMINATION\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Seed germination and its conditions\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different communication tools perfectly and explain the process of seed germination.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"seeds, soil, water, radio, computer, animation video\",\n    \"references\": \"Science and Elementary Technology Teacher’s guide for Primary four\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson introduces students to the concept of seed germination, its importance, and the conditions necessary for it to occur. Through a combination of engaging activities, experiments, and discussions, students will develop their understanding of the process and apply their knowledge to real-life scenarios.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured, and learners participated actively in the experiments and discussions. Most learners understood the concepts of seed germination and its conditions. Next time, I will include more visual aids and provide additional support for slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a farmer, and you want to grow crops, but you don\'t know how seeds germinate. What would you do?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to share their experiences with planting seeds\",\n            \"Teacher writes down key terms related to seed germination on the chalkboard\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to identify the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a diagram of a seed and asks learners to label its parts\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions about seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher uses radio to play a podcast about seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to discuss in pairs what they learned from the podcast\",\n            \"Teacher provides a worksheet with a crossword puzzle related to seed germination\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by sharing their thoughts and ideas\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as water, soil, and sunlight\",\n            \"Learners share their personal experiences with planting seeds\",\n            \"Learners copy the key terms into their notebooks\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to identify the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Learners label the parts of the seed diagram\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about seed germination\",\n            \"Learners listen to the podcast and take notes\",\n            \"Learners discuss in pairs what they learned from the podcast\",\n            \"Learners complete the crossword puzzle worksheet\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their thoughts and ideas\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners identify the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think about how to apply their knowledge of seed germination to real-life scenarios\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about the life cycle of a plant\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they plant seeds in different conditions\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to observe and record the changes in the seeds\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a diagram of the life cycle of a plant\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to identify the different stages of the life cycle\",\n            \"Teacher uses computer to show a simulation of seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to discuss in groups what they learned from the simulation\",\n            \"Teacher provides a worksheet with a chart to record the results of the experiment\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to analyze the data and draw conclusions\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions about the experiment\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the puzzle to find the correct order of the life cycle\",\n            \"Learners plant seeds in different conditions and observe the changes\",\n            \"Learners record the changes in the seeds and discuss the results\",\n            \"Learners identify the different stages of the life cycle\",\n            \"Learners watch the simulation and take notes\",\n            \"Learners discuss in groups what they learned from the simulation\",\n            \"Learners complete the chart to record the results of the experiment\",\n            \"Learners analyze the data and draw conclusions\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the experiment\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to present their findings\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners develop an interest in learning about seed germination\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners learn about the importance of plants in the environment\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of seed germination as the process by which a seed begins to grow\",\n            \"Teacher provides the definition of seed germination and explains its importance\",\n            \"Teacher uses diagrams to illustrate the process of seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to take notes on the definition and importance of seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a summary of the key points\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to identify the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher uses computer to show a video about seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to discuss in pairs what they learned from the video\",\n            \"Teacher provides a worksheet with a quiz about seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to complete the quiz\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition and importance of seed germination\",\n            \"Learners copy the summary of key points into their notebooks\",\n            \"Learners identify the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes\",\n            \"Learners discuss in pairs what they learned from the video\",\n            \"Learners complete the quiz\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about seed germination\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to present their understanding of seed germination\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they learned\",\n            \"Learners think about how to apply their knowledge of seed germination to real-life scenarios\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their thoughts and ideas\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners learn about the importance of seed germination in agriculture and its economic benefits\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design a garden and explain how they would ensure seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the importance of seed germination in agriculture\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to research and present on different types of seeds and their germination conditions\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a case study of a farm that uses seed germination techniques\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to analyze the case study and discuss in groups\",\n            \"Teacher uses computer to show a video about a farm that uses seed germination techniques\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to discuss in pairs what they learned from the video\",\n            \"Teacher provides a worksheet with a scenario where learners must apply their knowledge of seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to complete the scenario\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions about the project\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners design a garden and explain how they would ensure seed germination\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate and share their thoughts and ideas\",\n            \"Learners research and present on different types of seeds and their germination conditions\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and discuss in groups\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes\",\n            \"Learners discuss in pairs what they learned from the video\",\n            \"Learners complete the scenario\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the project\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to present their designs\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they learned\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design a garden and explain how they would ensure seed germination\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners learn about the importance of seed germination in different cultures\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question quiz: Q1: What is seed germination? Q2: What are the conditions necessary for seed germination? Q3: Why is seed germination important in agriculture? Q4: What are some common mistakes that can prevent seed germination? Q5: How can you ensure seed germination in your garden?\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Design a garden and explain how you would ensure seed germination. Write a short essay on the importance of seed germination in agriculture.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they learned\",\n            \"Teacher provides a worksheet with a self-assessment rubric\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to complete the self-assessment rubric\",\n            \"Teacher encourages learners to ask questions about the quiz or homework\",\n            \"Teacher uses computer to show a video about seed germination\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to discuss in pairs what they learned from the video\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a summary of the key points\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to review the summary\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions: Q1: Seed germination is the process by which a seed begins to grow. Q2: The conditions necessary for seed germination are water, soil, and sunlight. Q3: Seed germination is important in agriculture because it allows for the growth of new plants. Q4: Some common mistakes that can prevent seed germination are insufficient water, poor soil quality, and lack of sunlight. Q5: You can ensure seed germination in your garden by providing the necessary conditions and taking care of the seeds.\",\n            \"Learners complete the homework: Design a garden and explain how you would ensure seed germination. Write a short essay on the importance of seed germination in agriculture.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they learned\",\n            \"Learners complete the self-assessment rubric\",\n            \"Learners ask questions about the quiz or homework\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes\",\n            \"Learners discuss in pairs what they learned from the video\",\n            \"Learners review the summary\",\n            \"Learners think about how to apply their knowledge of seed germination to real-life scenarios\",\n            \"Learners evaluate their own learning\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the conditions necessary for seed germination\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take responsibility for their own learning\",\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners learn about the importance of seed germination in different cultures and its impact on society\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 12:11:58', '2026-01-30 12:11:58');
INSERT INTO `lesson_plans` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `content`, `version`, `generated_by_ai`, `ai_provider`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(31, 14, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with Visual impairment, These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"CALCULUS\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Integrating Using Long Division and Completing the Square.\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, calculators, and graph paper, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to integrate functions using long division and completing the square perfectly, given a function and a set of conditions.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Calculators, Computers, Graph paper\",\n    \"references\": \"Calculus textbook by James Stewart, Chapter 7\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"The lesson will start with an introduction to the concept of integration using long division and completing the square. The teacher will then guide the learners through a series of examples and exercises to help them understand the concept. The learners will then work in pairs to complete a set of exercises and finally, the teacher will summarize the key points and provide feedback.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts of integration using long division and completing the square. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A company has a cost function C(x) = 2x^2 + 5x + 3, where x is the number of units produced. The company wants to find the total cost of producing 10 units. How can we use integration to solve this problem?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute video on the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to brainstorm how they can use integration to solve real-world problems.\",\n            \"Teacher writes down the key terms and concepts on the board, such as integral, long division, and completing the square.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a diagram of the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the key elements, such as the cost function and the number of units produced.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key terms and concepts, such as integral, long division, and completing the square, and write them down in their notes.\",\n            \"Learners brainstorm how they can use integration to solve real-world problems, such as finding the area under a curve or the volume of a solid.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms and concepts, including the formulas and examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their ideas on how to use integration to solve real-world problems.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify the key elements, such as the cost function and the number of units produced.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use computers and calculators to explore the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with examples of integration using long division and completing the square, such as ∫(2x^2 + 5x + 3) dx.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they use calculators to evaluate the integral of a function, such as ∫(x^2 + 2x + 1) dx.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of exercises for learners to practice, such as ∫(3x^2 + 2x - 1) dx.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to use graph paper to visualize the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the examples and exercises to find the integral of a function, such as ∫(2x^2 + 5x + 3) dx.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their findings, such as the value of the integral.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete the set of exercises, such as ∫(3x^2 + 2x - 1) dx.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms and concepts, including the formulas and examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their time and resources to complete the exercises and experiments.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners consider the environmental impact of the company\'s production and how integration can be used to optimize resources.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of integration using long division and completing the square, such as ∫(2x^2 + 5x + 3) dx = (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + 3x + C.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula: ∫(ax^2 + bx + c) dx = (a/3)x^3 + (b/2)x^2 + cx + C and explains the concept of completing the square.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to use the formula to evaluate the integral of a function, such as ∫(x^2 + 2x + 1) dx.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of how to use integration to solve real-world problems, such as finding the area under a curve or the volume of a solid.\",\n            \"Teacher writes down the key terms and concepts on the board, such as integral, long division, and completing the square.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition of integration using long division and completing the square, such as ∫(2x^2 + 5x + 3) dx = (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + 3x + C.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to solve examples, such as ∫(x^2 + 2x + 1) dx.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete a set of exercises, such as ∫(3x^2 + 2x - 1) dx.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms and concepts, including the formulas and examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to use integration to solve real-world problems.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners consider the financial implications of the company\'s production and how integration can be used to optimize resources.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners reflect on how the concept of integration using long division and completing the square can be applied to real-world problems that affect different genders.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must use integration to solve a real-world problem, such as finding the area under a curve or the volume of a solid.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of integration on real-world problems, such as optimizing resources or predicting population growth.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a set of case studies for learners to analyze and apply the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to use technology, such as calculators or computers, to visualize and solve integration problems.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a solution to a real-world problem using integration, such as finding the area under a curve or the volume of a solid.\",\n            \"Learners present their arguments for or against the use of integration in real-world problems, such as optimizing resources or predicting population growth.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case studies and apply the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms and concepts, including the formulas and examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners reflect on the ethical implications of using integration to solve real-world problems.\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners consider the needs of different learners and how to adapt the concept of integration using long division and completing the square to meet those needs.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the case studies and apply the concept of integration using long division and completing the square to solve real-world problems.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is the integral of ∫(2x^2 + 5x + 3) dx? A) (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + 3x + C, B) (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + 2x + C, C) (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + x + C, D) (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + 4x + C. Q2: What is the formula for integration using long division and completing the square? A) ∫(ax^2 + bx + c) dx = (a/3)x^3 + (b/2)x^2 + cx + C, B) ∫(ax^2 + bx + c) dx = (a/2)x^3 + (b/3)x^2 + cx + C, C) ∫(ax^2 + bx + c) dx = (a/4)x^3 + (b/2)x^2 + cx + C, D) ∫(ax^2 + bx + c) dx = (a/2)x^3 + (b/4)x^2 + cx + C.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve problems 1-5 on the worksheet, such as ∫(3x^2 + 2x - 1) dx.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the learners\' performance and provides suggestions for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher summarizes the key points of the lesson, including the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A) (2/3)x^3 + (5/2)x^2 + 3x + C, Q2: Expected Answer: A) ∫(ax^2 + bx + c) dx = (a/3)x^3 + (b/2)x^2 + cx + C.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions for clarification.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms and concepts, including the formulas and examples.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on the concept of integration using long division and completing the square.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners manage their time and resources to complete the homework tasks.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners think creatively about how to apply the concept of integration using long division and completing the square to real-world problems.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 12:17:46', '2026-01-30 12:17:46'),
(32, 15, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with Social, Emotional \\u0026 Behavioral difficulties will be helped by using positive reinforcement, providing extra support during activities, and offering one-on-one guidance when needed. These students will also be helped by using visual aids and providing written instructions to supplement verbal explanations.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Programing with Java\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different programming concepts used in Java and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply Java programming concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Java Script programing\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers and Java programming software, every student will be able to write and execute a simple Java program perfectly, given the condition of having prior knowledge of basic programming concepts, with a degree of accuracy of at least 80%.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers with Java programming software, whiteboard, markers\",\n    \"references\": \"Java Programming textbook, chapters 3-5\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to Java Script programming, where they will learn to write and execute simple Java programs. The lesson will start with an introduction to Java Script, followed by a guided practice session where students will write their own Java programs. The lesson will conclude with an evaluation of the students\\u0027 understanding of Java Script programming.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-structured and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts of Java Script programming. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners and provide additional resources for further practice.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a game developer and you want to create a game that can be played on multiple platforms. How would you use Java Script to achieve this?\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a Java Script program being written and executed.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to brainstorm and discuss the following questions: What is Java Script? What are its advantages and disadvantages?\",\n            \"Teacher provides a brief overview of the history and development of Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the importance of Java Script in modern web development.\",\n            \"Teacher writes a simple Java Script program on the board and asks learners to identify the different components.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a list of Java Script keywords and asks learners to match them with their meanings.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the Java Script syntax and asks learners to identify the different parts.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of variables in Java Script and provides examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the key elements and thinking about how they can be applied to real-life situations.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as the use of variables, data types, and control structures.\",\n            \"Learners brainstorm and discuss the questions in small groups and present their answers to the class.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the history and development of Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and participate in a class discussion on the importance of Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different components of the Java Script program and explain their functions.\",\n            \"Learners match the Java Script keywords with their meanings and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script and present them to the class.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different parts of the Java Script syntax and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of how variables can be used in Java Script.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and present their answers to the class.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think about how to apply Java Script to real-life situations.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with a guided practice exercise on writing a simple Java Script program.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they write and execute a Java Script program.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a list of Java Script functions and asks learners to match them with their descriptions.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of conditional statements in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher writes a Java Script program on the board and asks learners to identify the different components.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the Java Script syntax and asks learners to identify the different parts.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of loops in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a list of Java Script keywords and asks learners to match them with their meanings.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a simple Java Script program and asks learners to modify it to perform a different task.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the guided practice exercise to find the solution.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their findings.\",\n            \"Learners match the Java Script functions with their descriptions and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of conditional statements in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different components of the Java Script program and explain their functions.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different parts of the Java Script syntax and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of how loops can be used in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners match the Java Script keywords with their meanings and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script and present them to the class.\",\n            \"Learners modify the Java Script program to perform a different task and test it.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners work independently to complete the guided practice exercise.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners learn about the different Java Script functions and their applications.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use computers to write and execute Java Script programs.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of Java Script programming by explaining the syntax and semantics.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for writing a simple Java Script program and explains it.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of variables in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher writes a Java Script program on the board and asks learners to identify the different components.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the Java Script syntax and asks learners to identify the different parts.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of conditional statements in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a list of Java Script functions and asks learners to match them with their descriptions.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of loops in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a simple Java Script program and asks learners to modify it to perform a different task.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of functions in Java Script and provides examples.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of Java Script programming.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to write a simple Java Script program.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of how variables can be used in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different components of the Java Script program and explain their functions.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different parts of the Java Script syntax and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of conditional statements in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners match the Java Script functions with their descriptions and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of how loops can be used in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners modify the Java Script program to perform a different task and test it.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of how functions can be used in Java Script.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners think about how to apply Java Script to real-life situations.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script.\",\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and present their answers to the class.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must write a Java Script program to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of Java Script on modern web development.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a list of Java Script functions and asks learners to match them with their descriptions.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of object-oriented programming in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher writes a Java Script program on the board and asks learners to identify the different components.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram of the Java Script syntax and asks learners to identify the different parts.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of event-driven programming in Java Script and provides examples.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a simple Java Script program and asks learners to modify it to perform a different task.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a case study of a company that uses Java Script and asks learners to analyze it.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a Java Script program to solve a real-world problem.\",\n            \"Learners participate in a debate on the impact of Java Script on modern web development.\",\n            \"Learners match the Java Script functions with their descriptions and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the concept of object-oriented programming in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different components of the Java Script program and explain their functions.\",\n            \"Learners identify the different parts of the Java Script syntax and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners provide examples of how event-driven programming can be used in Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners modify the Java Script program to perform a different task and test it.\",\n            \"Learners come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script and present them to the class.\",\n            \"Learners analyze the case study and provide recommendations for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Financial Education: Learners learn about the cost-benefit analysis of using Java Script in web development.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners learn about the environmental impact of using Java Script in web development.\",\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners learn about the ethical considerations of using Java Script in web development.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is Java Script? A) A programming language, B) A scripting language, C) A markup language, D) A database language. Q2: What is the purpose of the \\u0027var\\u0027 keyword in Java Script? A) To declare a variable, B) To declare a function, C) To declare a class, D) To declare an object. Q3: What is the difference between \\u0027null\\u0027 and \\u0027undefined\\u0027 in Java Script? A) \\u0027null\\u0027 is a primitive value, while \\u0027undefined\\u0027 is an object. B) \\u0027null\\u0027 is an object, while \\u0027undefined\\u0027 is a primitive value. C) \\u0027null\\u0027 is a primitive value, while \\u0027undefined\\u0027 is a reference to a non-existent object. D) \\u0027null\\u0027 is a reference to a non-existent object, while \\u0027undefined\\u0027 is a primitive value. Q4: What is the purpose of the \\u0027for\\u0027 loop in Java Script? A) To iterate over an array, B) To iterate over an object, C) To iterate over a string, D) To iterate over a number. Q5: What is the difference between \\u0027==\\u0027 and \\u0027===\\u0027 in Java Script? A) \\u0027==\\u0027 checks for value equality, while \\u0027===\\u0027 checks for reference equality. B) \\u0027==\\u0027 checks for reference equality, while \\u0027===\\u0027 checks for value equality. C) \\u0027==\\u0027 checks for value equality, while \\u0027===\\u0027 checks for both value and reference equality. D) \\u0027==\\u0027 checks for reference equality, while \\u0027===\\u0027 checks for both value and reference equality.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Write a Java Script program to solve a real-world problem. The program should include variables, conditional statements, loops, and functions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a rubric for assessing the homework assignment.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on what they learned in the lesson and what they would like to learn more about.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to learners on their participation and engagement during the lesson.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to provide feedback on the lesson and suggest improvements.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a summary of the key concepts learned in the lesson.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to think about how they can apply what they learned in the lesson to real-life situations.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a list of resources for further learning and practice.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the MCQ quiz questions and submit their answers.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework assignment and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners review the rubric for assessing the homework assignment and ask questions if they are unsure.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on what they learned in the lesson and what they would like to learn more about.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to the teacher on their participation and engagement during the lesson.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback on the lesson and suggest improvements.\",\n            \"Learners review the summary of the key concepts learned in the lesson.\",\n            \"Learners think about how they can apply what they learned in the lesson to real-life situations.\",\n            \"Learners review the list of resources for further learning and practice.\",\n            \"Learners come up with a list of potential applications of Java Script and present them to the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners learn about the importance of accessibility in web development.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners learn about the gender differences in the use of Java Script.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners learn about the importance of self-management and personal development in learning Java Script.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 12:23:26', '2026-01-30 12:23:26'),
(33, 15, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with Social, Emotional \\u0026 Behavioral difficulties. These students will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Programing with Java\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Java Script programing\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different communication tools perfectly, given the availability of computers and internet, with 90% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"laboratory\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, telephones, radio, and animation video\",\n    \"references\": \"Java Script programming textbook\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will cover the basics of Java Script programming, including variables, data types, and control structures. Students will learn how to write simple Java Script programs using computers and telephones. The lesson will include a combination of lectures, discussions, and hands-on activities to engage students and promote learning. By the end of the lesson, students will be able to identify and state the use of different communication tools perfectly.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was organized and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a web developer and you need to create a website that can interact with users. You will use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a web page that uses Java Script to interact with users.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to brainstorm and discuss the following questions: What is Java Script? What are its uses? How does it work?\",\n            \"Teacher writes down the students\\u0027 responses on the chalkboard and addresses any misconceptions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a brief overview of the lesson objectives and outcomes.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to share their prior knowledge and experience with Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher uses a radio connected to the computer to play an audio clip that explains the basics of Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a video that demonstrates how to write a simple Java Script program.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the following terms with their definitions: variable, data type, control structure.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to students as they work on the activity.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the key elements and asking questions.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as variables, data types, and control structures.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the brainstorming and discussion activity by sharing their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the key terms and concepts discussed during the introduction.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the terms with their definitions and ask for feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners use the radio connected to the computer to listen to the audio clip and take notes.\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes on how to write a simple Java Script program.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their prior knowledge and experience with Java Script and think about how they can apply it to the lesson.\",\n            \"Learners use the chalkboard to take notes and review the key terms and concepts.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the scenario and identify the key elements.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners brainstorm and come up with new ideas and solutions.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take notes and review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their prior knowledge and experience with Java Script and think about how they can apply it to the lesson.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with a puzzle about Java Script variables and data types.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they write a simple Java Script program using variables and data types.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the activity.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to solve a problem that requires the use of Java Script control structures.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a video that demonstrates how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support to learners as they work on the activity.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to present their web pages to the class and provide feedback.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the radio connected to the computer to play an audio clip that explains the basics of Java Script control structures.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the puzzle to find the solution and learn about Java Script variables and data types.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their findings.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the problem and learn about Java Script control structures.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes on how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners present their web pages to the class and receive feedback.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Learners use the chalkboard to review the key terms and concepts.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the puzzle and identify the solution.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take notes and review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners work in pairs and groups to promote collaboration and equality.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of Java Script variables and data types as follows: \\u0027A variable is a name given to a value. Data types determine the type of value that can be stored in a variable.\\u0027\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula: x = 5, where x is a variable and 5 is the value.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the concept of Java Script control structures as follows: \\u0027Control structures determine the flow of a program. They include if-else statements, for loops, and while loops.\\u0027\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to match the following terms with their definitions: if-else statement, for loop, while loop.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the activity.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the radio connected to the computer to play an audio clip that explains the basics of Java Script control structures.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a video that demonstrates how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support to learners as they work on the activity.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition of Java Script variables and data types.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to solve a problem.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the terms with their definitions and ask for feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes on how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Learners use the chalkboard to review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Learners use the radio connected to the computer to listen to the audio clip and take notes.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs and groups to promote collaboration and equality.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take notes and review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners think about how they can use Java Script to create interactive web pages that promote sustainability.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must design a simple web page that uses Java Script to interact with users.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of Java Script on web development.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance and support to learners as they work on the project.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to present their web pages to the class and provide feedback.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the radio connected to the computer to play an audio clip that explains the basics of Java Script and its applications.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a video that demonstrates how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the activity.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Learners participate in the debate and share their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the guidance and support provided by the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners present their web pages to the class and receive feedback.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any concepts they do not understand.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Learners use the chalkboard to review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Learners use the radio connected to the computer to listen to the audio clip and take notes.\",\n            \"Learners watch the video and take notes on how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to match the following terms with their definitions: if-else statement, for loop, while loop.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take notes and review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners participate in the debate and share their thoughts and ideas.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners think about how they can use Java Script to create interactive web pages that promote financial literacy.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is Java Script? A) A programming language, B) A web development tool, C) A database management system, D) A network protocol. Q2: What is the purpose of a variable in Java Script? A) To store a value, B) To perform a calculation, C) To display output, D) To get user input.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Write a simple Java Script program that uses variables and data types. Q3: What is the difference between a for loop and a while loop? A) A for loop is used for repetition, while a while loop is used for conditional statements. B) A for loop is used for conditional statements, while a while loop is used for repetition. C) A for loop is used for arrays, while a while loop is used for objects. D) A for loop is used for objects, while a while loop is used for arrays.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to solve a problem that requires the use of Java Script control structures. Q4: What is the purpose of an if-else statement in Java Script? A) To perform a calculation, B) To display output, C) To get user input, D) To make a decision. Q5: What is the difference between a Java Script variable and a Java Script constant? A) A variable can be changed, while a constant cannot be changed. B) A variable cannot be changed, while a constant can be changed. C) A variable is used for numbers, while a constant is used for strings. D) A variable is used for strings, while a constant is used for numbers.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback and guidance to learners as they work on the activity.\",\n            \"Teacher uses the radio connected to the computer to play an audio clip that explains the basics of Java Script and its applications.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a video that demonstrates how to use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with examples of Java Script programs that use control structures.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in groups to design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A) A programming language.\",\n            \"Learners answer Q2: Expected Answer: A) To store a value.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to solve the problem and learn about Java Script control structures.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask for feedback and guidance from the teacher.\",\n            \"Learners answer Q3: Expected Answer: A) A for loop is used for repetition, while a while loop is used for conditional statements.\",\n            \"Learners answer Q4: Expected Answer: D) To make a decision.\",\n            \"Learners answer Q5: Expected Answer: A) A variable can be changed, while a constant cannot be changed.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and think about how they can apply it to real-world situations.\",\n            \"Learners use the chalkboard to review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"Learners use the radio connected to the computer to listen to the audio clip and take notes.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners analyze the quiz questions and identify the correct answers.\",\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners work in pairs to solve the problem.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners design a simple web page that uses Java Script.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners take notes and review the key terms and concepts.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use Java Script to create interactive web pages.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 2, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 12:26:27', '2026-01-30 12:26:27');
INSERT INTO `lesson_plans` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `content`, `version`, `generated_by_ai`, `ai_provider`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(34, 16, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"No students with special needs identified.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"HEALTH LIVING\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define different terms used in the subject domain and use them in correct contexts.\\n. Apply concepts safely and responsibly.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"LANGUAGES STRUCTURE\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using computers, telephones, radio, and animation video, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the use of different language structures perfectly.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"smartclass\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, telephones, radio, animation video, whiteboard, markers\",\n    \"references\": \"English textbook, pages 100-105\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will cover the basics of language structure, including nouns, verbs, and adjectives. Students will learn to identify and use these structures correctly in sentences. The lesson will include a combination of lectures, group work, and interactive activities to engage students and promote learning.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was organized and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: Imagine you are a doctor and you need to explain a diagnosis to a patient. You need to use simple language to help the patient understand.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video on the importance of language structure in communication.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to brainstorm examples of how language structure is used in everyday life.\",\n            \"Teacher writes the examples on the board and asks learners to discuss in pairs.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with a list of language structures and asks learners to identify which ones they have used before.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to share their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a simple sentence and asks learners to identify the nouns, verbs, and adjectives.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to create their own sentences using different language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to provide guidance and answer questions.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to share their sentences with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the language structures used.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as nouns, verbs, and adjectives.\",\n            \"Learners brainstorm examples of how language structure is used in everyday life.\",\n            \"Learners discuss in pairs and share their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Learners identify the language structures on the handout and share their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Learners create their own sentences using different language structures.\",\n            \"Learners share their sentences with the class.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the language structures and examples discussed in class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and share their answers with the class.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners identify the key elements in the video and brainstorm examples of how language structure is used in everyday life.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with exercises on identifying nouns, verbs, and adjectives.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they have to create their own sentences using different language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to complete the exercises.\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to provide guidance and answer questions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the exercises and asks learners to revise their work.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to create a short paragraph using a variety of language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a list of vocabulary words and asks learners to use them in their paragraphs.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to share their paragraphs with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a rubric for assessing the paragraphs and asks learners to peer-assess each other\'s work.\",\n            \"Teacher collects the paragraphs and provides feedback.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the exercises to find the correct answers.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their findings.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to complete the exercises.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts.\",\n            \"Learners create a short paragraph using a variety of language structures.\",\n            \"Learners use the vocabulary words in their paragraphs.\",\n            \"Learners share their paragraphs with the class.\",\n            \"Learners peer-assess each other\'s work using the rubric.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the feedback and revise their work.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners create a short paragraph using a variety of language structures.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of language structure as the foundation of effective communication.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the definition of nouns, verbs, and adjectives and explains their functions.\",\n            \"Teacher uses examples to illustrate the correct usage of language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to take notes on the definitions and examples.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a diagram to illustrate the relationships between language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher explains the importance of using correct language structures in writing and speaking.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a list of common errors in language structure and asks learners to identify the correct forms.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in pairs to practice using the correct language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher circulates around the room to provide guidance and answer questions.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the practice exercises and asks learners to revise their work.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the definition of nouns, verbs, and adjectives.\",\n            \"Learners identify the functions of language structures and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners use the examples to practice identifying the correct language structures.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to practice using the correct language structures.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the common errors in language structure and the correct forms.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners use the diagram to illustrate the relationships between language structures.\",\n            \"Learners peer-assess each other\'s work using the rubric.\",\n            \"Learners revise their work based on the feedback.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners understand the importance of using correct language structures in writing and speaking.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must create a short story using a variety of language structures.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the impact of language structure on communication.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to work in groups to design a poster on the importance of language structure.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a list of vocabulary words and asks learners to use them in their stories and posters.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to share their stories and posters with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a rubric for assessing the stories and posters and asks learners to peer-assess each other\'s work.\",\n            \"Teacher collects the stories and posters and provides feedback.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance on how to improve the stories and posters.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to revise their work based on the feedback.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a poster on the importance of language structure.\",\n            \"Learners create a short story using a variety of language structures.\",\n            \"Learners use the vocabulary words in their stories and posters.\",\n            \"Learners share their stories and posters with the class.\",\n            \"Learners peer-assess each other\'s work using the rubric.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the feedback and revise their work.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts.\",\n            \"Learners use the feedback to improve their stories and posters.\",\n            \"Learners present their revised work to the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners work in groups to design a poster on the importance of language structure.\",\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use technology to create and present their stories and posters.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question multiple-choice quiz: Q1: What is the function of a noun in a sentence? A) To describe a verb, B) To describe a noun, C) To describe an adjective, D) To describe an adverb. Q2: What is the correct form of the verb \'to be\' in the present tense? A) Am, B) Is, C) Are, D) Be. Q3: What is the definition of an adjective? A) A word that describes a noun, B) A word that describes a verb, C) A word that describes an adjective, D) A word that describes an adverb. Q4: What is the importance of using correct language structures in writing and speaking? A) To communicate effectively, B) To confuse the reader, C) To make the text more difficult to understand, D) To make the text more interesting. Q5: What is the function of a verb in a sentence? A) To describe a noun, B) To describe a verb, C) To describe an adjective, D) To describe an adverb.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns homework: Write a short paragraph using a variety of language structures and identify the nouns, verbs, and adjectives used.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback on the quiz and homework and asks learners to revise their work.\",\n            \"Teacher collects the homework and provides feedback.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to peer-assess each other\'s work using the rubric.\",\n            \"Teacher provides guidance on how to improve the paragraphs.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to revise their work based on the feedback.\",\n            \"Teacher asks learners to present their revised work to the class.\",\n            \"Teacher evaluates the learners\' understanding of language structure and provides feedback.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer the quiz questions: Q1: B) To describe a noun, Q2: A) Am, Q3: A) A word that describes a noun, Q4: A) To communicate effectively, Q5: B) To describe a verb.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their learning and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the feedback and revise their work.\",\n            \"Learners peer-assess each other\'s work using the rubric.\",\n            \"Learners revise their work based on the feedback.\",\n            \"Learners present their revised work to the class.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek clarification on any doubts.\",\n            \"Learners evaluate their own understanding of language structure and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Learners set goals for further learning and improvement.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners evaluate their own understanding of language structure and identify areas for improvement.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners use language structures to communicate effectively and respectfully.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 12:29:01', '2026-01-30 12:29:01'),
(35, 2, '```\n{\n  \"header_details\": {\n    \"special_needs_provision\": \"1 student with visual impairment, 2 students with physical disabilities will be helped by using radio connected to the computer for the audio and video. Scaffold the slow learner through using multiple ways of learning either by using photos, videos, and written notes on chalkboard.\",\n    \"unit_title\": \"Introduction To Quadratic Equation\",\n    \"key_unit_competence\": \"To be able to:\\n. Define and identify the roots of a quadratic equation in the form of ax² + bx + c = 0.\\n. Apply the formula for sum and product of roots to solve problems.\",\n    \"lesson_title\": \"Summation and subtraction of roots\",\n    \"instructional_objective\": \"Using real-life examples and mathematical software, at the end of this lesson, every student will be able to identify and state the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation perfectly, given the equation in the form ax² + bx + c = 0, with 90% accuracy.\",\n    \"plan_for_class\": \"smartclass\",\n    \"learning_materials\": \"Computers, telephones, radio, and animation videos\",\n    \"references\": \"Mathematics textbook, pages 10-15\"\n  },\n  \"lesson_flow_overview\": \"This lesson will introduce students to the concept of sum and product of roots of a quadratic equation. Students will learn how to apply the formula for sum and product of roots to solve problems. The lesson will include a combination of lectures, discussions, and activities to engage students and promote understanding.\",\n  \"teacher_self_evaluation\": \"The lesson was well-organized, and learners participated actively. Most learners understood the concepts of sum and product of roots. Next time, I will include more examples and activities to support slower learners and provide additional visual aids to enhance understanding.\",\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"timing\": \"20 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Engage\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher presents this scenario: A farmer has 100 meters of fencing and wants to enclose a rectangular area. If the length of the rectangle is x meters, find the width in terms of x.\",\n            \"Teacher shows a 2-minute animation video of a quadratic equation in the form ax² + bx + c = 0 and asks students to identify the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to discuss in pairs how they can find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher writes the formula for sum and product of roots on the board: x₁ + x₂ = -b/a and x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a real-life example of a quadratic equation and asks students to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher uses mathematical software to demonstrate the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to work in pairs to match the quadratic equations with their corresponding sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with examples of quadratic equations and asks students to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Teacher reminds students of the importance of understanding the concept of sum and product of roots in solving quadratic equations.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners observe and discuss the scenario by identifying the variables and the constant term.\",\n            \"Learners identify the key elements in the video such as the coefficients of the quadratic equation.\",\n            \"Learners take notes on the formula for sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to find the sum and product of the roots of the given quadratic equation.\",\n            \"Learners use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to their peers on their work.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Communication and Collaboration: Learners discuss in pairs and provide feedback to their peers.\",\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners identify the variables and the constant term in the quadratic equation.\",\n            \"Gender Education: Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and activities.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Development\",\n      \"timing\": \"48 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explore\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides worksheets with examples of quadratic equations and asks students to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher guides learners through an experiment where they have to find the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation using different methods.\",\n            \"Teacher demonstrates how to use mathematical software to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with examples of quadratic equations and asks students to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to work in pairs and discuss their findings.\",\n            \"Teacher reminds students to use the formula for sum and product of roots: x₁ + x₂ = -b/a and x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional examples for students to practice.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Teacher reviews the key concepts and formulas with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners investigate the examples and find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Learners observe the experiment results and record their findings.\",\n            \"Learners use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to discuss their findings and provide feedback to their peers.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to their peers on their work.\",\n            \"Learners review the key concepts and formulas with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners use different methods to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Environmental and sustainability: Learners are encouraged to use recyclable materials and reduce waste.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Explain\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher formalizes the concept of sum and product of roots as: x₁ + x₂ = -b/a and x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Teacher provides the formula for sum and product of roots and explains the derivation.\",\n            \"Teacher uses mathematical software to demonstrate the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides examples of quadratic equations and asks students to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to work in pairs and discuss their findings.\",\n            \"Teacher reminds students to use the formula for sum and product of roots: x₁ + x₂ = -b/a and x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional examples for students to practice.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Teacher reviews the key concepts and formulas with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners take notes on the formula for sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners apply the formula to solve examples of quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Learners use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners work in pairs to discuss their findings and provide feedback to their peers.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to their peers on their work.\",\n            \"Learners review the key concepts and formulas with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Life-long learning: Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners are encouraged to use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Inclusive Education: Learners are encouraged to participate equally in the discussion and activities.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Elaborate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher assigns a project where learners must find the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation using different methods.\",\n            \"Teacher leads a debate on the importance of understanding the concept of sum and product of roots in solving quadratic equations.\",\n            \"Teacher provides a handout with examples of quadratic equations and asks students to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to work in pairs and discuss their findings.\",\n            \"Teacher reminds students to use the formula for sum and product of roots: x₁ + x₂ = -b/a and x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional examples for students to practice.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Teacher reviews the key concepts and formulas with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their project.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners work in groups to design a project to find the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation.\",\n            \"Learners present their arguments for the importance of understanding the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to their peers on their work.\",\n            \"Learners review the key concepts and formulas with the class.\",\n            \"Learners receive feedback from the teacher on their project.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"Critical Thinking and Problem Solving: Learners design a project to find the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation.\",\n            \"Creativity and Innovation: Learners use different methods to find the sum and product of the roots.\",\n            \"Peace and Values Education: Learners are encouraged to work in groups and respect each other\'s opinions.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"section_name\": \"Conclusion\",\n      \"timing\": \"12 min\",\n      \"sub_phases\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"Evaluate\",\n          \"teacher_activities\": [\n            \"Teacher provides a 5-question MCQ quiz: Q1: What is the formula for the sum of the roots of a quadratic equation? A) x₁ + x₂ = -b/a, B) x₁ + x₂ = b/a, C) x₁ + x₂ = -c/a, D) x₁ + x₂ = c/a. Q2: What is the formula for the product of the roots of a quadratic equation? A) x₁ * x₂ = c/a, B) x₁ * x₂ = -c/a, C) x₁ * x₂ = b/a, D) x₁ * x₂ = -b/a.\",\n            \"Teacher assigns Homework: Solve the following quadratic equations and find the sum and product of the roots: x² + 5x + 6 = 0, x² - 3x - 4 = 0.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their quiz and homework.\",\n            \"Teacher reviews the key concepts and formulas with the class.\",\n            \"Teacher encourages students to ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Teacher reminds students to use the formula for sum and product of roots: x₁ + x₂ = -b/a and x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Teacher provides additional examples for students to practice.\",\n            \"Teacher asks students to reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Teacher provides feedback to students on their understanding of the concept.\",\n            \"Teacher reviews the key concepts and formulas with the class.\"\n          ],\n          \"learner_activities\": [\n            \"Learners answer Q1: Expected Answer: A) x₁ + x₂ = -b/a, Q2: Expected Answer: A) x₁ * x₂ = c/a.\",\n            \"Learners record the homework tasks and ask questions if needed.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to their peers on their work.\",\n            \"Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Learners ask questions and seek help if needed.\",\n            \"Learners review the key concepts and formulas with the class.\",\n            \"Learners receive feedback from the teacher on their quiz and homework.\",\n            \"Learners review their notes and textbook for additional practice.\",\n            \"Learners provide feedback to their peers on their work.\"\n          ],\n          \"competences\": [\n            \"ICT and Digital Literacy: Learners use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Self-Management and Personal Development: Learners reflect on their understanding of the concept of sum and product of roots.\",\n            \"Financial Education: Learners are encouraged to use mathematical software to explore the concept of sum and product of roots.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```', 1, 1, 'groq', '2026-01-30 15:36:34', '2026-01-30 15:36:34');

